n 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p>7 May 2026<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">,&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;<br>\r\n  8:00AM (EDT) - 9:00AM (EDT)<br>\r\n  9:00AM (EDT) - 10:00AM (EDT)<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  <p>10:00AM (EDT) - 11:00AM (EDT)<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:7;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Round Of Interview</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Final Round</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:8;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Person</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p>8:00AM (EDT) - 9:00AM (EDT): Amit Kumar (Senior Manager, Data Engineering)<br>\r\n  9:00AM (EDT) - 10:00AM (EDT): Daniel Fernandez (Data Engineer II)<br>\r\n  10:00AM (EDT) - 11:00AM (EDT): Nikitha Patil Andhe (Data Engineer II)<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:9;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Type</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">Zoom</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:10;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Link</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n   <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n   </tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:11;mso-yfti-lastrow:yes;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview JD</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <h3 style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:3.75pt;margin-left:\r\n  0in;box-sizing:inherit;text-transform:capitalize\"><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(11, 31, 40);\">About the job<br>\r\n  Expedia Group brands power global travel for everyone, everywhere. We design\r\n  cutting-edge tech to make travel smoother and more memorable, and we create\r\n  groundbreaking solutions for our partners. Our diverse, vibrant, and\r\n  welcoming community is essential in driving our success.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Why Join Us?<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  To shape the future of travel, people must come first. Guided by our Values\r\n  and Leadership Agreements, we foster an open culture where everyone belongs,\r\n  differences are celebrated and know that when one of us wins, we all win.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  We provide a full benefits package, including exciting travel perks, generous\r\n  time-off, parental leave, a flexible work model (with some pretty cool\r\n  offices), and career development resources, all to fuel our employees\'\r\n  passion for travel and ensure a rewarding career journey. We’re building a\r\n  more open world. Join us.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Introduction to the team<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Enterprise Data Product at Expedia Group builds innovative products,\r\n  services, and tools to deliver high-quality data experiences for travelers,\r\n  partners, and our internal teams. A singular technology platform powered by\r\n  data and machine learning provides secure, differentiated, and personalized\r\n  experiences for the travelers and our partners that drive loyalty and\r\n  customer satisfaction.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  In This Role, You Will<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain software services and components\r\n  that contribute to Expedia Group’s customer and partner experiences<br>\r\n  Implement clean, maintainable code in collaboration with peers, using modern\r\n  engineering practices, code reviews, and version control to ensure\r\n  high-quality delivery<br>\r\n  Participate in system design, including low-level design (LLD), API design,\r\n  and data modeling, to build scalable, reliable, and observable systems and\r\n  services<br>\r\n  Troubleshoot and resolve issues across the software development lifecycle,\r\n  contributing to incident resolution, root cause analysis, and continuous\r\n  improvement of service reliability<br>\r\n  Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand requirements, break\r\n  down work into executable tasks, and deliver features that can be reused\r\n  across multiple domains and products<br>\r\n  Safely integrate and operate AI/ML enabled solutions that improve outcomes,\r\n  including familiarity with AI-driven systems, tools, or workflows and\r\n  applying AI/ML concepts to real world products<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Minimum Qualifications<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related technical field; or\r\n  Equivalent related professional experience<br>\r\n  2+ years of relevant professional experience<br>\r\n  Experience owning components or services within a broader system, including\r\n  responsibility for implementation quality, basic operational support, and\r\n  participation in on-call or incident response as appropriate<br>\r\n  Proficiency in core computer science fundamentals (data structures,\r\n  algorithms, object-oriented design) and in designing and consuming APIs and\r\n  data models<br>\r\n  Familiarity with AI-driven systems, tools, or workflows and ability to safely\r\n  integrate AI/ML enabled capabilities into existing services under guidance<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Preferred Qualifications<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Experience designing and implementing low-level designs, APIs, and data\r\n  models for services that operate at scale, including considerations for\r\n  performance, reliability, and observability<br>\r\n  Demonstrated ability to contribute to architecture discussions within a team\r\n  or domain, including evaluating tradeoffs, proposing technical approaches,\r\n  and aligning with established patterns<br>\r\n  Experience integrating or extending AI/ML enabled capabilities in production\r\n  systems in a safe, compliant, and cost-effective way, such as using AI-driven\r\n  tools for testing, coding assistance, or personalization features<br>\r\n  Exposure to working across multiple product or service domains, with\r\n  demonstrated adaptability to new technologies, stacks, or problem spaces and\r\n  a growing ability to apply AI/ML concepts to real world products<br>\r\n  Strong understanding of batch + incremental processing patterns, including\r\n  backfills, data quality validation, and failure recovery<br>\r\n  Ability to build and evolve data pipelines with high data quality standards,\r\n  including validation, lineage, and SLA management<br>\r\n  Experience working with distributed data systems (e.g., Spark, Trino,\r\n  Iceberg) and optimizing for performance and cost<br>\r\n  Familiarity with API-first or data-as-a-product approaches, enabling reusable\r\n  and discoverable datasets<br>\r\n  Familiarity with streaming technologies like Apache Kafka or Apache\r\n  Flink&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></h3>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">&nbsp;</span></p>', '2026-05-07', '00:00:00', '01:00:00', '2026-05-07 18:34:44', '2026-05-07 19:34:21', 0, '2026-05-07 14:43:51', 4000.00, 1, 'UPI', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'task-262@bsquareg', NULL, 'completed');
