\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Round Of Interview</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p>Final Round<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:8;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Person</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\"></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:9;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Type</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p>Microsoft Teams<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:10;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Link</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n   <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n   </tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:11;mso-yfti-lastrow:yes;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview JD</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Job Description Summary<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  We are seeking an experienced IT Workday Configuration Analyst with hands-on\r\n  payroll processing experience. Someone in this role partners closely with the\r\n  operations payroll team to design, configure, and maintain Workday’s payroll,\r\n  absence, and time-tracking functionality to ensure accuracy, compliance, and\r\n  smooth end-to-end processing. They translate business requirements into\r\n  system configurations, troubleshoot issues, and optimize workflows so payroll\r\n  operations can run reliably and efficiently.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  The ideal candidate has processed payroll end-to-end, understands\r\n  gross-to-net calculations, tax setup, pay components, absence rules, and has\r\n  the technical aptitude to build, test, and maintain the Aeon Workday\r\n  solution.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Responsibilities<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Job Description <br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Workday Configuration &amp; Support<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &nbsp;Configure, maintain, and optimize Workday Payroll and Workday Absence,\r\n  including pay components, earnings, deductions, and time-off plans.<br>\r\n  &nbsp;Develop and update business processes, calculated fields, condition\r\n  rules, validation rules, and security related to Payroll and Absence.<br>\r\n  &nbsp;Partner with cross-functional IT and HR teams to ensure configuration\r\n  aligns with business requirements and Workday best practices.<br>\r\n  &nbsp;Troubleshoot system issues and support payroll operations by\r\n  identifying root causes and recommending process or configuration\r\n  improvements.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Testing &amp; Deployment<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &nbsp;Create and execute test plans for enhancements, patches, and Workday\r\n  releases.<br>\r\n  &nbsp;Validate payroll results, retro calculations, gross-to-net, taxes, and\r\n  off-cycle runs—to ensure post-configuration accuracy.<br>\r\n  &nbsp;Support bi-annual Workday releases by analyzing impacts, conducting\r\n  regression testing, and adopting new functionality.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Project &amp; Stakeholder Management<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &nbsp;Translate business requirements into clear, actionable system\r\n  specifications and configuration solutions.<br>\r\n  &nbsp;Work with payroll and absence partners to ensure Workday setup complies\r\n  with federal, state, and local tax and labor regulations as they provide\r\n  those changing requirements.<br>\r\n  &nbsp;Provide guidance and training to HR, Payroll, and operational teams on\r\n  Workday functionality, configuration changes, and process impacts.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Qualifications<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Bachelor’s degree or equivalent education/experience, preferably in IT or a\r\n  business area discipline (i.e. accounting, investments, or marketing).\r\n  Minimum of 5 or more years of experience in business systems analysis. 2-4\r\n  years of industry experience also preferred. Two years of experience managing\r\n  technical projects in a complex environment.<br>\r\n  Hands-on payroll processing experience (e.g., calculating payroll, resolving\r\n  payroll issues, managing pay periods, supporting audits, handling\r\n  garnishments, validating taxes). This experience is essential to\r\n  understanding payroll scenarios when configuring Workday.<br>\r\n  Strong knowledge of U.S. payroll concepts, including earnings, deductions,\r\n  taxes, retroactivity, off-cycle payments, gross-to-net processing, year-end\r\n  activities, and compliance.<br>\r\n  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with attention to detail and\r\n  data accuracy.<br>\r\n  Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, collaborative environment.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Preferred Qualifications<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Workday experience would be ideal but not required; candidates with strong\r\n  payroll processing experience and a willingness to complete Workday training\r\n  will be considered.<br>\r\n  Experience supporting multi-state payroll environments.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Key Competencies<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Proven experience with end-to-end payroll processing, balancing, and issue\r\n  resolution.<br>\r\n  Solid gross-to-net knowledge, including earnings, deductions, and taxes.<br>\r\n  Ability to troubleshoot payroll exceptions and perform root cause analysis.<br>\r\n  Skilled in reconciliation, audit readiness, and maintaining data accuracy.<br>\r\n  Understanding of how time, absence, and benefits impact payroll.<br>\r\n  Knowledge of garnishments and third-party payments.<br>\r\n  Clear, professional communication and strong customer service orientation.<br>\r\n  Process-improvement mindset with a focus on accuracy and efficiency.<br>\r\n  High level of confidentiality and integrity with sensitive pay data.<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>', '2026-05-12', '23:30:00', '00:30:00', NULL, NULL, 0, '2026-05-12 15:12:52', 4000.00, 1, 'UPI', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'completed'),
