 5.4pt;height:33.65pt;border-color:currentcolor windowtext windowtext\">\r\n  <p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Candidate&nbsp;Number</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"padding:0in 0in 0in 0in;height:33.65pt\"></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:4;mso-yfti-lastrow:yes;height:33.65pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"420\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:314.85pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.65pt;border-color:currentcolor windowtext windowtext currentcolor\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\">+1 (217) 610-2029<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"padding:0in 0in 0in 0in;height:33.65pt\"></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Present<span style=\"letter-spacing:-.25pt\">&nbsp;</span>Location<span style=\"letter-spacing:\r\n-.25pt\">&nbsp;</span>with<span style=\"letter-spacing:-.25pt\">&nbsp;</span>zip<span style=\"letter-spacing:-.25pt\">&nbsp;</span>code</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Northlake,\r\n</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Google Sans&quot;;color:#001D35\">Texas&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">76262</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Company\r\nName</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<h3 style=\"line-height:15.0pt;margin:inherit;text-overflow:ellipsis;overflow:\r\nhidden\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Google Sans&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:#1F1F1F\">walmart</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Google Sans&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Interview&nbsp;Date\r\n&amp; Time</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Google Sans&quot;;\r\ncolor:#1F1F1F;background:#F0F4F9\">Tue 12 May 2026<br>\r\n</span>03:15 PM - 04:00 PM<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Round\r\nOf&nbsp;Interview</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Technical<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Interview&nbsp;Person</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:47.25pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"> </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Monalisha Jena<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:47.25pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"> </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Babasaheb Sawant<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:47.25pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;color:black\">·<span style=\"font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"> </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Edgar Gonzalez<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Interview&nbsp;Type</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Ms Teams&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Interview&nbsp;Link&nbsp;\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px;\">\r\n <tbody><tr>\r\n  <td width=\"540\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:405.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n  <div align=\"center\">\r\n  <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px;\">\r\n   <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:0in 0in 14.25pt 0in;border-spacing:0px\">\r\n    <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:14.25pt\"><b><span style=\"font-family:\r\n    &quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hacker Rank Url :&nbsp;</span></b><a href=\"https://hr.gs/8068825\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\">https://hr.gs/8068825</span></a><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n    <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"left\" width=\"543\" style=\"width: 407.05pt; border-spacing: 0px;\">\r\n     <tbody><tr>\r\n      <td style=\"padding:0in 0in 0in 0in\"></td>\r\n     </tr>\r\n    </tbody></table>\r\n    </td>\r\n   </tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\r\n <tbody><tr>\r\n  <td width=\"540\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:405.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n  <div align=\"center\">\r\n  <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\r\n   <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:0in 0in 0in 0in\"></td>\r\n   </tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"xmsonormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Interview&nbsp;JD</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">About the job<br>\r\nPosition Summary...Building the right technology foundation for Infrastructure\r\n&amp; platforms is vital to success at the scale of Walmart. Our team builds\r\nand maintains the foundational technologies that support the tech organization.\r\nIncluded in this are data platforms, enterprise architecture, DevOps, cloud\r\ncomputing, and infrastructure. All of these products and services are supported\r\nby scalable and powerful infrastructure, ensuring a secure and seamless\r\nemployee and customer experience across stores, digital channels, and\r\ndistribution centers.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWhat you\'ll do...Join Walmart Global Tech\'s Data Platform Services organization\r\nas an Edge Cloud Computing System - Software Engineer II to develop Edge cloud\r\ndatabase systems that autonomously monitor, predict, and resolve issues across\r\nthe world\'s largest retailer\'s technology ecosystem, impacting millions of\r\ncustomers and associates globally. You\'ll lead the transformation of\r\ntraditional Database Managing/Supporting practices into cutting-edge, self-healing\r\nplatforms that serve as the intelligent backbone for database administration\r\nacross all of Walmart\'s systems, from e-commerce to stores to supply chain.\r\nWhat you\'ll do: You’ll contribute to building and supporting reliable database\r\nplatforms that help power Walmart’s stores and facilities. You’ll work with\r\nexperienced engineers to implement technical solutions and tools for Walmart\r\nTechnology teams across various channels and geographies. Database Engineering\r\n&amp; Solution Delivery:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nAssist in developing and maintaining database solutions and platforms for\r\nWalmart’s<br>\r\ntechnology ecosystem. <br>\r\nHelp implement architecture patterns for scalability, maintainability, and<br>\r\nperformance. <br>\r\nSupport the creation of observability and monitoring interfaces for anomaly\r\ndetection and analytics. <br>\r\nParticipate in building APIs for edge database solutions and integrating with\r\noperational systems. <br>\r\n<br>\r\nEngineering Excellence &amp; Code Quality:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWrite code that is readable, maintainable, and efficient, following team\r\nstandards. <br>\r\nApply best practices for testing, performance optimization, and monitoring. <br>\r\nHelp develop automation and agents using AI technologies as guided by senior\r\nengineers. <br>\r\nTroubleshoot and resolve basic performance issues in distributed applications. <br>\r\nAssist with CI/CD pipelines for database systems, including deployment and\r\nvalidation. <br>\r\nLearn and adopt new technologies and frameworks as part of your growth. <br>\r\n<br>\r\nCollaboration &amp; Teamwork:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWork closely with engineering partners and cross-functional teams to deliver\r\nsolutions. <br>\r\nParticipate in code reviews, technical discussions, and documentation. <br>\r\nCollaborate with designers and product managers to improve user experience. <br>\r\nEngage in a culture of learning, asking questions, and sharing knowledge. <br>\r\n<br>\r\nWhat You\'ll Work With:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nDatabase platforms: MariaDB, Postgres, Informix (nice to have but not\r\nmandatory),<br>\r\nTools &amp; languages: Ansible, Python, Shell scripting, Java,\r\nJavaScript/TypeScript, GitHub, Kubernetes, Looper<br>\r\nModern frontend tooling and testing framework<br>\r\nCI/CD systems such as Jenkins<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWhat you\'ll bring:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science/Engineering or equivalent experience<br>\r\n1+ years of experience as a software engineer<br>\r\nFamiliarity with Python, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript, GoLang, and Ansible<br>\r\nExperience with React or similar JavaScript frameworks is a plus<br>\r\nUnderstanding of containerization and Kubernetes is helpful<br>\r\nExposure to RDBMS database architecture (e.g., Postgres, MariaDB)<br>\r\nBasic understanding of caching, logging, performance tuning, and monitoring<br>\r\nExperience with GitHub and version control best practices<br>\r\nExposure to unit testing and CI/CD systems such as Jenkins<br>\r\nComfortable working in a distributed team and communicating asynchronously<br>\r\nEagerness to learn, collaborate, and grow within the team<br>\r\n<br>\r\nAbout Walmart Global Tech<br>\r\n<br>\r\nImagine working in an environment where one line of code can make life easier\r\nfor hundreds of millions of people. That’s what we do at Walmart Global Tech.\r\nWe’re a team of software engineers, data scientists, cybersecurity expert\'s and\r\nservice professionals within the world’s leading retailer who make an epic\r\nimpact and are at the forefront of the next retail disruption. People are why\r\nwe innovate, and people power our innovations. We are people-led and\r\ntech-empowered. We train our team in the skillsets of the future and bring in\r\nexperts like you to help us grow. We have roles for those chasing their first\r\nopportunity as well as those looking for the opportunity that will define their\r\ncareer. Here, you can kickstart a great career in tech, gain new skills and\r\nexperience for virtually every industry, or leverage your expertise to innovate\r\nat scale, impact millions and reimagine the future of retail. Walmart’s culture\r\nis a competitive advantage, and it’s fostered by being together. Working\r\ntogether in person allows us to collaborate, align quickly and innovate with\r\ngreater speed. We use our campuses to create purposeful connection rooted in\r\ndeepening understanding and investing in the development of our associates.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nOur hubs: Walmart is a global company with offices across the United States and\r\naround the world. Our global headquarters is in Bentonville, Arkansas, with\r\nprimary hubs in the San Francisco Bay area and New York/New Jersey.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBenefits:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBenefits: Beyond our great compensation package, you can receive incentive\r\nawards for your performance. Other great perks include 401(k) match, stock\r\npurchase plan, paid maternity and parental leave, PTO, multiple health plans,\r\nand much more.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nEqual Opportunity Employer:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWalmart, Inc. is an Equal Opportunity Employer – By Choice. We believe we are\r\nbest equipped to help our associates, customers, and the communities we serve\r\nlive better when we really know them. That means understanding, respecting, and\r\nvaluing unique styles, experiences, identities, ideas, and opinions – while\r\nbeing inclusive of all people.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThe above information has been designed to indicate the general nature and\r\nlevel of work performed in the role. It is not designed to contain or be\r\ninterpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all responsibilities and\r\nqualifications required of employees assigned to this job. The full Job\r\nDescription can be made available as part of the hiring process.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nAt Walmart, we offer competitive pay as well as performance-based bonus awards\r\nand other great benefits for a happier mind, body, and wallet. Health benefits\r\ninclude medical, vision and dental coverage. Financial benefits include 401(k),\r\nstock purchase and company-paid life insurance. Paid time off benefits include\r\nPTO (including sick leave), parental leave, family care leave, bereavement,\r\njury duty, and voting. Other benefits include short-term and long-term\r\ndisability, company discounts, Military Leave Pay, adoption and surrogacy\r\nexpense reimbursement, and more. You will also receive PTO and/or PPTO that can\r\nbe used for vacation, sick leave, holidays, or other purposes. The amount you\r\nreceive depends on your job classification and length of employment. It will\r\nmeet or exceed the requirements of paid sick leave laws, where applicable. For\r\ninformation about PTO, see <a href=\"https://one.walmart.com/notices\" target=\"_blank\">https://one.walmart.com/notices</a>. Live Better U is a\r\nWalmart-paid education benefit program for full-time and part-time associates\r\nin Walmart and Sam\'s Club facilities. Programs range from high school\r\ncompletion to bachelor\'s degrees, including English Language Learning and\r\nshort-form certificates. Tuition, books, and fees are completely paid for by\r\nWalmart.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nEligibility requirements apply to some benefits and may depend on your job\r\nclassification and length of employment. Benefits are subject to change and may\r\nbe subject to a specific plan or program terms.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nFor Information About Benefits And Eligibility, See One.Walmart.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThe annual salary range for this position is $80,000.00 - $155,000.00\r\nAdditional compensation includes annual or quarterly performance bonuses.\r\nAdditional compensation for certain positions may also include :<br>\r\n<br>\r\nStock<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Malgun Gothic&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Aptos;color:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">ㅤ</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Malgun Gothic&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Aptos;color:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">ㅤ</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Malgun Gothic&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Aptos;color:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">ㅤ</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Malgun Gothic&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Aptos;color:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">ㅤ</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#0A0A0A;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n‎<br>\r\n<br>\r\nMinimum Qualifications...<br>\r\n<br>\r\nOutlined below are the required minimum qualifications for this position. If\r\nnone are listed, there are no minimum qualifications. <br>\r\n<br>\r\nOption 1: Bachelor\'s degree in computer science, computer engineering, computer\r\ninformation systems, software engineering, or related area.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nOption 2: 3 years’ experience in software engineering or related area.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nPreferred Qualifications...<br>\r\n<br>\r\nOutlined below are the optional preferred qualifications for this position. If\r\nnone are listed, there are no preferred qualifications.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWe value candidates with a background in creating inclusive digital\r\nexperiences, demonstrating knowledge in implementing Web Content Accessibility\r\nGuidelines (WCAG) 2.2 AA standards, assistive technologies, and integrating\r\ndigital accessibility seamlessly. The ideal candidate would have knowledge of\r\naccessibility best practices and join us as we continue to create accessible\r\nproducts and services following Walmart’s accessibility standards and\r\nguidelines for supporting an inclusive culture.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nPrimary Location...<br>\r\n<br>\r\n2403 Se J St, Bentonville, AR 72716, United States of America<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWalmart and its subsidiaries are committed to maintaining a drug-free workplace\r\nand has a no tolerance policy regarding the use of illegal drugs and alcohol on\r\nthe job. This policy applies to all employees and aims to create a safe and\r\nproductive work environment.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBenefits found in job post<br>\r\n<br>\r\n401(k)<br>\r\n<!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br>\r\n<!--[endif]--></span>', '2026-05-12', '00:45:00', '01:30:00', '2026-05-12 19:18:12', '2026-05-12 19:38:28', 45, '2026-05-12 15:14:50', 6800.00, 1, 'UPI', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'task-299@bsquareg', NULL, 'completed');
