;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Round Of Interview</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Preperation</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:8;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Person</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\"></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:9;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Type</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:10;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Link</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n   <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n   </tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:11;mso-yfti-lastrow:yes;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview JD</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><br>\r\n  Amazon Job Description<br>\r\n  Are you looking for that next big Finance opportunity? Do you want to\r\n  directly influence the future of AWS by helping make the right investment\r\n  decisions? AWS Finance seeks a Senior Financial Analyst to join the AWS\r\n  Regions Finance team.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  In AWS Regions we develop strategies for infrastructure in new countries,\r\n  look 10+ years down the road, oversee current region build-outs across new,\r\n  launched, and ADC regions, and review performance of existing regions through\r\n  their life-cycle. We work closely with senior leaders in cross-functional\r\n  partner organizations developing and reviewing the strategic multi-billion\r\n  infrastructure investments.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  You will drive strategic FP&amp;A initiatives including controllership\r\n  functions, region-grain analytics, and Risks &amp; Opportunities (R&amp;O)\r\n  including efficiency metrics to improve the quality and timelines of business\r\n  insights provided to AWS and Amazon leadership, including ongoing efforts\r\n  around existing process improvements.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  If you want to join a fast-paced, innovative team that is making history,\r\n  this is the place for you. To build this rapidly growing business, you must\r\n  be highly analytical, strategic, detail-oriented, and set high standards for\r\n  accuracy and pace.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  This position will be responsible for driving monthly financial reviews and\r\n  OP planning for early-stage and ADC regions, identifying key insights by\r\n  connecting dots between various infra drivers across the business. The role\r\n  will perform core FP&amp;A and controllership functions including\r\n  region-grain P&amp;L management, R&amp;O identification and tracking\r\n  (efficiency metrics, cost optimization opportunities), and financial\r\n  performance analysis.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  The role will also support regions-wide consolidation and advisory, and drive\r\n  several AWS-wide mechanisms in partnership with central and tech teams.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  This role regularly interfaces with leaders of AWS Regions Finance,\r\n  Infrastructure Finance, Accounting, Sales &amp; Strategy teams and provides\r\n  business and financial insights on regional performance that gets reported to\r\n  AWS and Amazon senior leadership.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Key job responsibilities<br>\r\n  - Drive core financial processes including annual operating plans,\r\n  monthly/quarterly business reviews and assessment of risks/opportunities, and\r\n  month-end close.<br>\r\n  - Influence strategy through effective verbal and written communication of\r\n  financial metrics and business drivers to senior finance and business\r\n  leadership<br>\r\n  - Work cross functionally with other AWS Finance teams and senior leadership\r\n  on forecasting quarter-end/ annual/ multi-year performance<br>\r\n  - Help prepare and deliver business reviews to the senior management team\r\n  regarding progress and potential roadblocks in the execution of new region\r\n  expansion plans<br>\r\n  - Perform financial reporting, ad-hoc project analysis and financial modeling\r\n  to support business and finance leadership<br>\r\n  - Identify and lead special projects to drive automation and process\r\n  improvement, collaborating with other AWS Finance partner teams<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Basic Qualifications<br>\r\n  - 4+ years of tax, finance or a related analytical field experience<br>\r\n  - 4+ years of applying key financial performance indicators (KPIs) to\r\n  analyses experience<br>\r\n  - Bachelor\'s degree in finance, accounting, business, economics, or a related\r\n  analytical field (e.g., engineering, math, computer science)<br>\r\n  - 4+ years of building financial and operational reports/data sets that\r\n  inform business decision-making experience<br>\r\n  - 3+ years of dissecting financial data and identifying patterns that support\r\n  business strategy experience<br>\r\n  - 3+ years of contributing to cross-functional initiatives that drive\r\n  financial performance and strategy experience<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Preferred Qualifications<br>\r\n  - 4+ years of participating in continuous improvement projects in your team\r\n  to scale and improve controllership with measurable results experience<br>\r\n  - 4+ years of identifying, leading, and executing opportunities to improve,\r\n  automate, standardize or simplify finance or business tools and processes\r\n  experience<br>\r\n  - 4+ years of dissecting financial data and identifying patterns that support\r\n  business strategy experience<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Amazon is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the\r\n  basis of protected veteran status, disability, or other legally protected\r\n  status.<br>\r\n  <!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br>\r\n  <!--[endif]--><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  <h3 style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:3.75pt;margin-left:\r\n  0in\"><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;\r\n  mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:#0B1F28;font-weight:normal\">Trantor\r\n  Company Job Description<o:p></o:p></span></h3>\r\n  <h3 style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:3.75pt;margin-left:\r\n  0in;box-sizing:inherit;text-transform:capitalize\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n  18.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\n  color:#0B1F28;font-weight:normal\">1. Must-Have Experience (Non-Negotiable)<br>\r\n  Deep Domain Mastery (Workday Adaptive / Anaplan):<br>\r\n  The \"Why\": These platforms have proprietary logic and unique data\r\n  structures (cubes, dimensions, versions).<br>\r\n  Required Skills: Ability to architect multi-dimensional models, manage\r\n  \"what-if\" scenarios, and automate data flows from ERPs (like\r\n  Netsuite/Oracle) into Adaptive/Anaplan.<br>\r\n  Anaplan Sub: If using Anaplan, they must understand Level 2/3 Model Building\r\n  principles (e.g., DISCO methodology).<br>\r\n  Agentic Frameworks (Python-Based):<br>\r\n  Required Skills: Hands-on experience with LangGraph, CrewAI, or LangChain to\r\n  build multi-agent workflows (e.g., an agent that\r\n  \"Plan-Executes-Validates\" a budget variance report).<br>\r\n  API &amp; Integration Expertise:<br>\r\n  Required Skills: Advanced knowledge of REST APIs for Workday Extend or\r\n  Anaplan Connect. The candidate must be able to write the \"tools\"\r\n  that an AI agent uses to pull live data or write back adjusted forecasts.<o:p></o:p></span></h3>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>', '2026-05-29', '02:35:00', '03:05:00', '2026-05-29 23:01:33', '2026-05-29 23:01:48', 0, '2026-05-29 16:06:00', 0.00, 1, 'UPI', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'task-527@bsquareg', NULL, 'completed');
