r\n  - 11:30<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"> </span>PM EST<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:7;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Round Of Interview</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Screening with Director</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:8;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Person</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\"></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:9;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Type</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:10;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Link</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n   <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n   </tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:11;mso-yfti-lastrow:yes;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview JD</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n  Job Description : This role combines financial planning, data analytics, and\r\n  systems leadership to support strategic decision-making and operational\r\n  excellence across the HSB business units and functions. The analyst will lead\r\n  validation efforts for Oracle PCM, develop advanced Power BI models, and\r\n  co-lead AI initiatives that enhance forecasting, reporting, and automation.\r\n  The role requires strong cross-functional collaboration across the finance\r\n  organization and a deep understanding of financial systems, data\r\n  architecture, and analytical tools. Respond to ad hoc requests supporting\r\n  internal initiatives. Optimize process flows, streamline data workflows, and\r\n  enhance reporting. Develop automation, conduct QA, and perform data\r\n  validations to ensure efficiency, and reliability across reporting systems.<br>\r\n  Education and Experience:<br>\r\n  Bachelor’s Degree in Accounting, Finance or equivalent work experience<br>\r\n  7+ years progressive FP&amp;A or Analytics experience<br>\r\n  Strong operational background<br>\r\n  Advanced Excel skills (including macros, pivot tables, and complex formulas).<br>\r\n  Strong Power BI experience (data modeling, DAX, dashboard design).<br>\r\n  Python experience preferred<br>\r\n  Familiarity with EPM tools such as Oracle Enterprise Planning Management\r\n  (SmartView, Workforce Planning) is a plus.<br>\r\n  Strong data mining, engineering and analysis skills<br>\r\n  Some business-facing background preferred<br>\r\n  Knowledge and Skills:<br>\r\n  HSB experience<br>\r\n  Strong operational accounting / Finance expertise and critical thinking\r\n  skills<br>\r\n  Experience working with business teams and analyzing business results<br>\r\n  Strong project management, leadership, communication and negotiation skills<br>\r\n  Ability to work and influence cross-functionally and ensure stakeholder\r\n  requirements are satisfied<br>\r\n  Ability to think abstractly in order to be able to link divergent programs\r\n  and processes<br>\r\n  Strong interpersonal skills – written, verbal and listening<br>\r\n  Ability to work independently and in a team<br>\r\n  At The Hartford Steam Boiler, a subsidiary of Munich Re, we see Diversity and\r\n  Inclusion as a solution to the challenges and opportunities all around us.\r\n  Our goal is to foster an inclusive culture and build a workforce that\r\n  reflects the customers we serve and the communities in which we live and\r\n  work. We strive to provide a workplace where all of our colleagues feel\r\n  respected, valued and empowered to achieve their very best every day. We\r\n  recruit and develop talent with a focus on providing our customers the most\r\n  innovative products and services.&nbsp; &nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>', '2026-06-03', '20:30:00', '21:00:00', '2026-06-03 14:46:09', '2026-06-03 15:38:45', 52, '2026-06-03 14:43:39', 4000.00, 1, 'UPI', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'task-573@bsquareg', NULL, 'completed'),
(574, 9, 229, 6, 1, 4, 'NA', '<div>About the job</div><div>Embark on a transformative journey as a Senior Full Stack Trading Floor Engineer. At Barclays, our vision is clear –to redefine the future of banking and help craft innovative solutions. In this role you will work directly with traders to build and enhance niche, high-impact tools used in real-time decision making. You will have the opportunity to work closely on the trading floor, gaining direct exposure to front-office workflows. This role sits at the intersection of trading, technology, and rapid innovation, offering the opportunity to shape solutions that directly influence business outcomes. You will take full ownership of applications, driving both new development and continuous improvement in a fast-paced environment.</div><div><br></div><div>To be successful as a Senior Full Stack Trading Floor Engineer, you should:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Demonstrate considerable ownership and accountability, taking end-to-end responsibility for development, delivery, and support of applications</div><div>Be comfortable working in a dynamic, front-office environment with a focus on rapid issue resolution and adaptability to changing priorities</div><div>Have experience building and supporting production-ready full stack applications</div><div>Possess ample problem-solving and debugging skills, with the ability to identify root causes and resolve complex issues efficiently</div><div>Communicate effectively with traders and stakeholders to understand requirements and deliver impactful solutions</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Other Highly Valued Skills Include</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Experience with JavaScript, with additional experience in Python, ASP.NET, React, and KDB</div><div>Experience designing and implementing web service architectures</div><div>Ability to work on and support legacy systems, including delivering enhancements and continuous improvements</div><div>Understanding of banking workflows and front-office processes</div><div>Experience working with modern web technologies and frameworks</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>You may be assessed on the key critical skills relevant for success in role, such as risk and controls, change and transformation, business acumen, strategic thinking, digital and technology, as well as job-specific technical skills.</div><div><br></div><div>This role is located in our New York, NY office.</div><div><br></div><div>Minimum Salary: $120,000</div><div><br></div><div>Maximum Salary: $ 175,000</div><div><br></div><div>The minimum and maximum salary/rate information above includes only base salary or base hourly rate. It does not include any other type of compensation or benefits that may be available.</div><div><br></div><div>Purpose of the role</div><div><br></div><div>To design, develop and improve software, utilising various engineering methodologies, that provides business, platform, and technology capabilities for our customers and colleagues.</div><div><br></div><div>Accountabilities</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Development and delivery of high-quality software solutions by using industry aligned programming languages, frameworks, and tools. Ensuring that code is scalable, maintainable, and optimized for performance.</div><div>Cross-functional collaboration with product managers, designers, and other engineers to define software requirements, devise solution strategies, and ensure seamless integration and alignment with business objectives.</div><div>Collaboration with peers, participate in code reviews, and promote a culture of code quality and knowledge sharing.</div><div>Stay informed of industry technology trends and innovations and actively contribute to the organization’s technology communities to foster a culture of technical excellence and growth.</div><div>Adherence to secure coding practices to mitigate vulnerabilities, protect sensitive data, and ensure secure software solutions.</div><div>Implementation of effective unit testing practices to ensure proper code design, readability, and reliability.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Assistant Vice President Expectations</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>To advise and influence decision making, contribute to policy development and take responsibility for operational effectiveness. Collaborate closely with other functions/ business divisions.</div><div>Lead a team performing complex tasks, using well developed professional knowledge and skills to deliver on work that impacts the whole business function. Set objectives and coach employees in pursuit of those objectives, appraisal of performance relative to objectives and determination of reward outcomes</div><div>If the position has leadership responsibilities, People Leaders are expected to demonstrate a clear set of leadership behaviours to create an environment for colleagues to thrive and deliver to a consistently excellent standard. The four LEAD behaviours are: L – Listen and be authentic, E – Energise and inspire, A – Align across the enterprise, D – Develop others.</div><div>OR for an individual contributor, they will lead collaborative assignments and guide team members through structured assignments, identify the need for the inclusion of other areas of specialisation to complete assignments. They will identify new directions for assignments and/ or projects, identifying a combination of cross functional methodologies or practices to meet required outcomes.</div><div>Consult on complex issues; providing advice to People Leaders to support the resolution of escalated issues.</div><div>Identify ways to mitigate risk and developing new policies/procedures in support of the control and governance agenda.</div><div>Take ownership for managing risk and strengthening controls in relation to the work done.</div><div>Perform work that is closely related to that of other areas, which requires understanding of how areas coordinate and contribute to the achievement of the objectives of the organisation sub-function.</div><div>Collaborate with other areas of work, for business aligned support areas to keep up to speed with business activity and the business strategy.</div><div>Engage in complex analysis of data from multiple sources of information, internal and external sources such as procedures and practises (in other areas, teams, companies, etc).to solve problems creatively and effectively.</div><div>Communicate complex information. \'Complex\' information could include sensitive information or information that is difficult to communicate because of its content or its audience.</div><div>Influence or convince stakeholders to achieve outcomes.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>All colleagues will be expected to demonstrate the Barclays Values of Respect, Integrity, Service, Excellence and Stewardship – our moral compass, helping us do what we believe is right. They will also be expected to demonstrate the Barclays Mindset – to Empower, Challenge and Drive – the operating manual for how we behave.</div>', '2026-06-03', '20:30:00', '21:30:00', '2026-06-03 14:59:09', '2026-06-03 15:21:51', 22, '2026-06-03 14:46:53', 4000.00, 1, 'UPI', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'task-574@bsquareg', NULL, 'completed'),
