d width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p>June 5th, 2026, 11:30 AM- 12:30 PM EST<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:7;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Round Of Interview</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:34.75pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;2nd Round\r\n  Technical</b></span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:8;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Person</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\"></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:9;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Type</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">Teams</span><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:10;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview Link</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n   <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n   </tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow:11;mso-yfti-lastrow:yes;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Interview JD</span></b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"265\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:198.7pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;height:33.25pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\">SUMMARY<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  At Magnolia, the Senior Financial Analyst serves as the primary finance\r\n  business partner for an assigned business channel, owning the full FP&amp;A\r\n  cycle including budgeting, forecasting, variance analysis, and cash flow\r\n  forecasting. The position delivers accurate, timely financial reporting and\r\n  insights to support informed decision-making, identify risks and\r\n  opportunities, and improve financial performance. The Senior Financial\r\n  Analyst also contributes to the continuous improvement of financial processes\r\n  and controls by identifying opportunities and supporting analytical tools\r\n  that strengthen future planning. This position works from Magnolia\r\n  Headquarters in Waco, Texas. It reports to the Director of Finance and has no\r\n  supervisory responsibilities.<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Serve as the primary finance business partner for an assigned business\r\n  channel, owning the full FP&amp;A cycle including budgeting, forecasting,\r\n  variance analysis, and ad hoc financial support for channel leadership*<br>\r\n  Lead the analysis of historical and forward-looking financial data within the\r\n  assigned channel to surface insights, identify risks and opportunities, and\r\n  support informed business decisions<br>\r\n  Own and manage quarterly budget forecasts and monthly variance reporting\r\n  distributed to management across the company*<br>\r\n  Produce and own monthly budget versus actual financial statements, delivering\r\n  accurate and timely reporting in support of finance leadership*<br>\r\n  Maintain and continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of the 17-week\r\n  cash flow forecast*<br>\r\n  Serve as a day-to-day resource for assigned business channel, providing\r\n  detailed GL reporting and researching and resolving budgetary questions*<br>\r\n  Audit GL account activity and independently identify anomalies in the monthly\r\n  financials that may indicate breakdowns in departmental policies and\r\n  procedures; escalate findings with recommended next steps<br>\r\n  Develop ad hoc financial reports and analysis in support of finance\r\n  leadership’s reporting and decision-making needs<br>\r\n  Identify opportunities to improve finance processes, reporting tools, and\r\n  internal controls; escalate recommendations to the Director of Finance for\r\n  review and implementation<br>\r\n  Design, build, and maintain databases of pertinent financial information,\r\n  including analytical reports used in evaluating future plans and forecasts<br>\r\n  Perform other duties as assigned<br>\r\n  *Metrics evaluated on Performance Review<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  COMPETENCIES<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Teamwork: Contribute to a team environment supporting diversity, equity,\r\n  inclusion, and belonging. Work effectively with others, be a team player and\r\n  contribute toward team goals.<br>\r\n  Critical Thinking: Propose creative solutions within specific specialization.\r\n  Ability to analyze data, trends, and patterns.<br>\r\n  Expertise: Expert in knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques relevant to\r\n  specialization. Able to develop expertise in related area(s).<br>\r\n  Communication: Actively engage in listening to teammates and guests and be\r\n  open to feedback from guests, peers, and management.<br>\r\n  Guest Focus: Ability to proactively understand and meet guest needs, ensuring\r\n  a personalized and guest-centric experience.<br>\r\n  Strategy and Goal Setting: Approach change with positivity and curiosity.\r\n  Know your role in achieving team goals.<br>\r\n  Hard skills: Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel required, including\r\n  financial modeling, complex formulas, and data analysis. Experience using\r\n  NetSuite accounting software and Workday Adaptive Insights planning tool\r\n  strongly preferred. Comprehensive understanding of financial statements and\r\n  the accounting relationships among them. Strong command of financial metrics,\r\n  cash flow management, and FP&amp;A best practices including budgeting,\r\n  forecasting, and variance analysis.<br>\r\n  ELIGIBILITY QUALIFICATIONS<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  Bachelor\'s degree in Accounting, Finance, or Business Administration from a\r\n  4-year college or university preferred<br>\r\n  2-4 years of experience with a related degree, 4-7 years of experience with a\r\n  non-related degree, or 5+ years of industry experience preferred<br>\r\n  3–5 years of progressive experience in financial analysis, FP&amp;A,\r\n  accounting, or a related field required<br>\r\n  Demonstrated ability to independently own recurring financial deliverables\r\n  and business channel reporting<br>\r\n  Experience working cross-functionally with non-finance stakeholders\r\n  preferred.<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>', '2026-06-05', '21:00:00', '22:00:00', '2026-06-05 15:30:32', '2026-06-05 16:26:26', 55, '2026-06-05 14:55:11', 4000.00, 1, 'UPI', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'task-631@bsquareg', NULL, 'completed');
