(58, 159, 11, 'Next steps would be to keep her profile on hold for roles aligned with her visa status and reach out when a suitable opportunity becomes available.', '2026-04-29 14:09:30'),
(59, 161, 10, 'Cancelled', '2026-04-29 14:12:07'),
(60, 162, 7, 'Candidate communicated well, demonstrated strong fundamentals, and handled situational questions confidently. Limited exposure to domain-specific tools, but showed willingness to learn.', '2026-04-29 15:32:12'),
(61, 160, 11, 'Interview Rescheduled.', '2026-04-29 15:54:41'),
(62, 164, 11, 'Interview went well. She showed strong techno functional profile with good hands on experience in SAP MM and EWM, along with a solid BASIS background that helps in troubleshooting and integration understanding. She communicated clearly, gave practical examples, and showed a good understanding of real business processes, though full end to end ownership exposure can be strengthened further.\nNext steps would be to move her to the next round for deeper evaluation, focusing on full lifecycle project ownership, advanced EWM scenarios, and client facing capabilities to assess readiness for more independent or lead roles.', '2026-04-29 17:10:29'),
(63, 165, 8, 'done', '2026-04-29 17:20:40'),
(64, 163, 15, 'The interview went well. The candidate showed backend fundamentals, particularly in caching, rate limiting, and system design, with a solid production-oriented mindset. They effectively identified key challenges such as consistency, scalability, and failure handling.', '2026-04-29 17:43:44'),
(65, 167, 7, 'Candidate performed well with strong technical fundamentals and real-world experience. Demonstrated good ownership, system design thinking, and clear communication.', '2026-04-29 18:06:30'),
(66, 166, 9, 'Candidate join by himself in interview meeting.', '2026-04-29 18:58:30'),
(67, 168, 10, 'interview want well. candidate has good knowledge of technology and projects', '2026-04-29 20:27:11'),
(68, 169, 9, 'Task has been completed.', '2026-04-29 21:02:57'),
(69, 170, 7, 'Interview went well. Candidate communicated clearly, showed good practical knowledge, and demonstrated strong site experience. Likely to move forward to next round.', '2026-04-29 21:54:01'),
(70, 171, 11, 'Completed', '2026-04-30 14:01:59'),
(71, 174, 7, 'No support is needed for this round; it’s a normal HR discussion about the next steps and what to expect in the upcoming round.', '2026-04-30 15:25:40'),
(72, 172, 8, 'second round of interview', '2026-04-30 16:08:24'),
(73, 173, 10, 'candidate need confidence while speaking he was nervous in coding round', '2026-04-30 16:18:27'),
(74, 176, 9, '1st round done.', '2026-04-30 16:57:04'),
(75, 175, 7, 'The candidate communicated clearly and approached the problem in a structured way.\nShe initially used a greedy approach and later explored a dynamic programming solution based on hints, but the final implementation did not pass all test cases.', '2026-04-30 17:06:37'),
(76, 178, 15, 'Rescheduled', '2026-04-30 18:28:02'),
(77, 177, 8, 'screening', '2026-04-30 18:38:32'),
(78, 182, 9, 'Screening.', '2026-04-30 20:17:16'),
(79, 179, 11, 'Strong Data Engineer with solid hands-on experience in building scalable pipelines, working with cloud platforms, and handling real-world data challenges. Communicates clearly, understands both technical and business aspects, and shows a practical, problem-solving mindset.\nNext steps: Proceed with final technical/round discussion with the team, followed by feedback consolidation and decision. If aligned, move forward with offer discussion.', '2026-04-30 20:27:35'),
(80, 183, 7, 'This was a screening call for a remote contract opportunity. The role requires a mid to senior developer with strong .NET experience and deeper hands-on AI development, not just AI tool usage.', '2026-04-30 20:35:11'),
(81, 184, 11, 'The candidate showed DevOps experience, especially around cloud, Kubernetes, and LLM integrations, and is able to explain real-world scenarios with practical understanding.\n\nHowever, he should listen more carefully to the support person’s instructions, stay more structured, and be more confident and clear while delivering his answers to make a stronger impact.', '2026-04-30 21:00:35'),
(82, 181, 8, 'cancel', '2026-04-30 21:19:04'),
(83, 180, 10, 'interview went well', '2026-04-30 21:20:07'),
(84, 185, 11, 'Strong Data Engineer with solid hands-on experience in Databricks, Spark, and building scalable pipelines in regulated environments; communicates clearly, shows ownership, and aligns well with the modernization goals of the project.\n\nNext steps: Send SF-85 details and security screening instructions, share crosswalk template for completion, confirm salary flexibility internally, then schedule technical discussion with Program Manager and follow up with client interview.', '2026-05-01 15:23:40'),
(85, 186, 7, 'interview went well; the discussion focused on AWS, Terraform, ArgoCD, Dynatrace, and handling production incidents with observability and rollback strategies.\nThe candidate explained concepts with relevant real-time examples and followed the support person’s guidance while answering.\nOverall, the candidate performed confidently with solid practical knowledge, though a few answers could be more crisp and structured.', '2026-05-01 15:49:34'),
(86, 187, 9, 'Coding Round.', '2026-05-01 16:38:28'),
(87, 188, 9, 'Screening Round.', '2026-05-01 17:22:24'),
(88, 189, 7, 'Screening call went well, focused on candidate’s experience managing multiple workstreams, stakeholder communication, and ability to influence without authority.\nInterviewer also explored work environment preference, accountability, and how the candidate builds trust across diverse teams.\nCandidate responded clearly with relevant examples, showing good alignment with a fast-paced, stakeholder-heavy role.', '2026-05-01 17:25:21'),
(89, 194, 10, 'Interview went well. The candidate was confident whole giving answers and also was interactive with interviewer', '2026-05-01 18:33:29'),
(90, 195, 7, 'interview went well overall. The discussion focused mainly on API design, request and response handling, validation, and exception handling in Spring Boot. The candidate was able to explain concepts clearly and corrected mistakes when prompted, showing good understanding.\n\nThere were a few gaps in initial implementation details like proper endpoint mapping and exception handling, but the candidate adapted quickly with guidance and improved the approach.', '2026-05-01 18:51:19'),
(91, 196, 9, 'interviewer didn\'t join.', '2026-05-01 18:52:55'),
(92, 198, 15, 'It’s just a screening round.', '2026-05-01 19:20:04'),
(93, 201, 9, 'Done.', '2026-05-01 20:56:03'),
(94, 199, 11, 'Interview went well. The candidate showed strong practical knowledge in AI/ML engineering, especially around RAG systems, data pipelines, and production considerations like latency, re-ranking, and guardrails. Communication was clear and structured, with good real-world examples, though a bit more crispness in some explanations would make responses even stronger.\n\nNext steps: The team will review feedback across interviewers and get back within a few days regarding the outcome or any further rounds, which may include deeper technical or client-focused discussions.', '2026-05-01 21:11:01'),
(95, 197, 11, 'For Monday', '2026-05-01 21:11:27'),
(96, 204, 8, 'screening', '2026-05-01 21:23:34'),
(97, 200, 15, 'The interview went well. It was a screening round where the interviewer asked both technical and behavioral questions. The candidate was able to explain the answers clearly and confidently.', '2026-05-01 21:29:10'),
(98, 202, 9, 'Done.', '2026-05-01 21:29:27'),
(99, 203, 10, 'interview went well, it was just a screening round', '2026-05-04 14:15:14'),
(100, 209, 7, 'Interview went average. Candidate communicated clearly with the interviewer and demonstrated decent understanding of geotechnical concepts.\n\nInterviewers emphasized quick joining as an important factor, and early June timeline was acceptable.\n\nThey mentioned they will discuss internally and get back with next steps.', '2026-05-04 17:07:54'),
(101, 212, 8, 'techincal', '2026-05-04 18:14:18'),
(102, 214, 10, 'Interview was well need some confidence while speaking', '2026-05-04 18:37:26'),
(103, 206, 8, 'technical', '2026-05-04 19:04:59'),
(104, 215, 11, 'Interview Link not received.', '2026-05-04 19:18:08'),
(105, 211, 11, 'The candidate comes across as a strong, well-rounded SAP SCM consultant with a solid mix of functional and technical experience, especially with the added advantage of a BASIS background. She communicates clearly, shows good ownership, and demonstrates practical, real-world problem-solving ability.\nShe would benefit from going slightly deeper into niche areas like EWM advanced capabilities, TM, or Ariba, and sharpening her positioning as a specialist to stand out further in mid-market SAP transformations.', '2026-05-04 19:18:31'),
(106, 213, 11, 'Completed', '2026-05-04 19:30:22'),
(107, 216, 7, 'Interview went average overall, with solid fundamentals and clear communication.\nShe handled iOS concepts well, while the coding round could have been more structured and concise.\nOverall performance was average, with room to improve confidence and conciseness.', '2026-05-04 21:11:09'),
(108, 217, 10, 'Interview went well. candidate gave answers perfectly', '2026-05-05 13:35:05'),
