(146, 262, 7, 'Interview went average overall. The candidate had good technical knowledge and relevant project experience, but while delivering answers it felt a little overacted and less natural at times.\n\nThe responses were technically correct, but the communication style needs to be more calm, conversational, and genuine instead of sounding overly prepared or performative.\n\nWith more natural delivery and smoother communication, the overall interview presence would become much stronger.', '2026-05-07 19:34:21'),
(147, 252, 11, 'Interview went well. She showed strong analytical thinking, good understanding of A/B testing, SQL, dashboard scalability, and stakeholder-driven reporting concepts. Communication was clear and structured throughout the interview, and the candidate showed practical problem-solving ability with a collaborative approach toward business and technical discussions.\nNext Steps: The interview feedback will be shared with the recruiting team and hiring panel for further evaluation. If shortlisted, the candidate will be contacted regarding the next round of discussions and process updates.', '2026-05-07 19:56:55'),
