(149, 260, 15, 'The interview went very well. The candidate communicated in a calm, confident, and professional manner throughout the discussion. He showed a solid understanding of distributed systems, effective collaboration practices, and key engineering trade-offs. His responses were practical, well-structured, and grounded in real-world project experience. He also handled behavioral and situational questions thoughtfully and naturally, without sounding overly rehearsed or scripted.', '2026-05-07 20:43:22'),
(150, 253, 11, 'Interview went well. Mayur showed practical experience in MLOps, Kubernetes, streaming systems, and production ML infrastructure. He was able to explain real-world deployment, monitoring, model versioning, and troubleshooting scenarios confidently, with good understanding of distributed systems and platform engineering concepts in whiteboard exercise.\n\nNext Steps: The interview feedback will be discussed internally with the team to evaluate the best fit across the available role tracks. HR will connect with the candidate regarding the final decision and potential next round discussions.', '2026-05-07 21:20:39'),
(151, 267, 16, 'Candidate had limited understanding of some advanced technologies and project sections initially. I explained the complete RUC document, technical skills, project architecture, workflows, and sprint structure step by step in detail, and the candidate was able to understand the concepts and project flow much better afterward.', '2026-05-08 15:43:35'),
