(95, 344, 0, 'Technical Assessment', 'StaffSource', 'N/A', 5, 5, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'He showed strong hands-on knowledge in AI/ML concepts, especially around LLMs, RAG pipelines, and practical problem-solving approaches. He communicated clearly throughout the discussion, stayed composed during technical questions, and showed a good balance of technical depth and real-world engineering understanding.', '', 4.50, '2026-05-21 14:44:24', '2026-05-21 14:44:24'),
(96, 343, 0, '2', 'Concoracredit', 'N/A', 5, 5, 4, 5, 'Yes', 'He showed strong hands-on knowledge in Databricks, Spark optimization, SQL execution flow, and distributed processing concepts. He communicated his thought process well, handled follow-up technical questions confidently, and showed practical production experience rather than just theoretical understanding. He performed especially well in explaining performance tuning tradeoffs, join strategies, and large-scale data processing scenarios. A small area for improvement would be giving slightly more concise answers in a few deep technical discussions, but overall, the candidate came across as technically solid, collaborative, and experienced for a senior data engineering role.', '', 4.75, '2026-05-21 14:46:24', '2026-05-21 14:46:24'),
(97, 264, 0, '2', 'hudsonmanpower', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Mayur showed practical experience in MLOps, Kubernetes, streaming systems, and production ML infrastructure. He was able to explain real-world deployment, monitoring, model versioning, and troubleshooting scenarios confidently, with good understanding of distributed systems and platform engineering concepts in whiteboard exercise. Next Steps: The interview feedback will be discussed internally with the team to evaluate the best fit across the available role tracks. HR will connect with the candidate regarding the final decision and potential next round discussions.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 14:49:09', '2026-05-21 14:49:09'),
(98, 253, 0, '', 'Capgemini', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. He presented experience with GenAI, RAG pipelines, LangChain workflows, and enterprise AI implementation. He explained technical concepts clearly with practical production examples and showed a good balance of backend engineering and AI integration knowledge.\n\nNext steps would be internal technical evaluation and client alignment discussion before scheduling the final round with the hiring team.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 14:50:42', '2026-05-21 14:50:42'),
(99, 252, 0, '2', 'Turing', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. She showed strong analytical thinking, good understanding of A/B testing, SQL, dashboard scalability, and stakeholder-driven reporting concepts. Communication was clear and structured throughout the interview, and the candidate showed practical problem-solving ability with a collaborative approach toward business and technical discussions.\nNext Steps: The interview feedback will be shared with the recruiting team and hiring panel for further evaluation. If shortlisted, the candidate will be contacted regarding the next round of discussions and process updates.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 14:51:44', '2026-05-21 14:51:44'),
(100, 237, 0, '2', 'Comcast', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went ok. He showed solid hands-on understanding of OCR pipelines, combining text extraction with coordinate-based mapping and practical use of NER and transformers when needed. He communicated his approach clearly and showed good production awareness, though he could improve by making his answers slightly more structured and concise at times. The interviewer was asking questions not related to his area of domain.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 14:53:05', '2026-05-21 14:53:05'),
(101, 232, 0, '1', 'Comcast', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. He showed hands-on experience with production ML systems, especially around model lifecycle, PySpark pipelines, and RAG-based LLM solutions. Communication was clear and practical, showing good understanding of real-world trade-offs, though deeper detail on Cat Boost-specific optimization and existing model debugging could strengthen the profile.\n Next Steps: Move forward to the final round with a 1-hour technical interview including a live coding exercise (Python/PySpark) and discussion on maintaining and improving existing production ML models.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 14:53:47', '2026-05-21 14:53:47'),
(102, 227, 0, '2', 'Infosys', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. He showed strong practical knowledge in AI/ML engineering, especially around RAG systems, data pipelines, and production considerations like latency, re-ranking, and guardrails. Communication was clear and structured, with good real-world examples, though a bit more crispness in some explanations would make responses even stronger.\n\nNext steps: The team will review feedback across interviewers and get back within a few days regarding the outcome or any further rounds, which may include deeper technical or client-focused discussions.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 14:54:38', '2026-05-21 14:54:38'),
(103, 211, 0, 'Final', 'Accenture', 'N/A', 4, 4, 5, 4, 'Yes', 'The candidate comes across as a strong, well-rounded SAP SCM consultant with a solid mix of functional and technical experience, especially with the added advantage of a BASIS background. She communicates clearly, shows good ownership, and demonstrates practical, real-world problem-solving ability.\nShe would benefit from going slightly deeper into niche areas like EWM advanced capabilities, TM, or Ariba, and sharpening her positioning as a specialist to stand out further in mid-market SAP transformations.', '', 4.25, '2026-05-21 14:56:29', '2026-05-21 14:56:29'),
(104, 199, 0, '', 'RUSH', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. He presented himself as strong Data Engineer with solid hands-on experience in building scalable pipelines, working with cloud platforms, and handling real-world data challenges. Communicated clearly, understands both technical and business aspects, and shows a practical, problem-solving mindset.\n\nNext steps: Proceed with final technical/round discussion with the team, followed by feedback consolidation and decision. If aligned, move forward with offer discussion.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 14:57:11', '2026-05-21 14:57:11'),
(105, 185, 0, '2', 'Infosys', 'N/A', 4, 5, 4, 5, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. He showed strong practical knowledge in AI/ML engineering, especially around RAG systems, data pipelines, and production considerations like latency, re-ranking, and guardrails. Communication was clear and structured, with good real-world examples, though a bit more crispness in some explanations would make responses even stronger.\n\nNext steps: The team will review feedback across interviewers and get back within a few days regarding the outcome or any further rounds, which may include deeper technical or client-focused discussions.', '', 4.50, '2026-05-21 14:58:52', '2026-05-21 14:58:52'),
