(139, 335, 0, '2', 'Origami Risk', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'She showed strong analytical thinking and communicated business concepts well, especially around franchise economics, forecasting, and investment tradeoff discussions. She came across as thoughtful and collaborative, with solid FP&A and data analytics experience that aligned well with the role requirements.\nAt times, some responses felt slightly guided or overly polished, likely because she was using the HurdleMate AI support tool during the discussion, but overall she handled the conversation confidently and showed good business understanding and problem-solving ability.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-21 22:23:54', '2026-05-21 22:23:54'),
(140, 276, 0, '2', 'Lean Layer', 'N/A', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The candidate demonstrated strong analytical thinking, solid RevOps and BI fundamentals, and communicated complex pipeline and attainment insights in a clear business-focused way. She showed good ownership of the analysis, explained technical logic confidently, and handled follow-up questions thoughtfully, especially around root-cause analysis, dashboard design, and AI usage. One area to improve would be tighter QA and attention to presentation-level details, since the attainment percentage formatting issue slightly impacted executive-readiness of the case study. Overall, the candidate came across as technically capable, collaborative, and well-aligned for a client-facing BI and RevOps analytics role.', '', 3.00, '2026-05-21 22:25:37', '2026-05-21 22:25:37'),
