(194, 486, 0, '1', 'micro1', 'AI interviewer', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. It was an AI interview. He showed strong practical knowledge in SSL/TLS hardening, firewall enforcement, and cryptographic best practices. He explained technical concepts clearly with a good balance of security reasoning, operational impact, and real-world implementation experience.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-28 16:13:19', '2026-05-28 16:13:19'),
(195, 483, 0, '2', 'Dominion', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. He presented strong hands-on experience in Data Engineering concepts, especially around SQL, Spark, dimensional modeling, production support, CI/CD, and cloud-based pipeline development. He communicated confidently, showed good problem-solving ability during the SQL and modeling discussions, and appeared adaptable with a strong learning mindset despite limited exposure to Talend specifically.\nNext steps would be to complete the remaining candidate evaluations over the next 1 to 2 weeks and shortlist top candidates for final consideration. If selected for the next round, the recruiter or hiring team will reach out with further details regarding follow-up discussions and team alignment.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-28 16:32:09', '2026-05-28 16:32:09'),
(196, 496, 0, '1', 'Nordstrom', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Aritra Shom showed hands-on full stack experience with React, Java Spring Boot, microservices, AWS, and distributed systems. He explained real production scenarios confidently, especially around API design, async workflows, scalability, and frontend-backend integration, while showing good ownership and practical problem-solving skills.\n\nCommunication was natural and technical depth was solid overall, though some answers could be slightly more structured and concise during system design discussions. Overall, the candidate showed good engineering maturity and appears capable of contributing effectively in a modern full stack microservices environment.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-28 18:36:03', '2026-05-28 18:36:03'),
(197, 491, 0, 'Technical + Coding Round', 'Molex', 'Isaac Kroger, Nick Agne', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'No', 'Need deeper hands-on exposure with Python desktop frameworks like PyQT and lower-level hardware communication concepts. Could improve unit testing discussions and provide more structured verification strategies during implementation discussions.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-28 19:04:50', '2026-05-28 19:04:50'),
