(204, 495, 0, '1', 'razrhq', 'N/A', 2, 2, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'Interview went ok. He showed hands-on knowledge of AWS, DevOps operations, monitoring, infrastructure automation, and production support. He tried to communicate practical real-world experience well, especially around cloud infrastructure, CI/CD, monitoring, and database availability concepts, and showed a good attitude toward learning new technologies like Pulumi.\n\nHowever, he needs to work on his communication fluency during interviews. At times, he stammered and fumbled while answering technical questions, which affected the confidence and clarity of his responses even when he knew the concepts well.', '', 2.00, '2026-05-28 20:34:56', '2026-05-28 20:34:56'),
(205, 501, 0, '1', 'Fiserv', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Prachi communicated very confidently throughout the discussion and showed strong product ownership, especially around payments workflows, roadmap prioritization, stakeholder management, and data-driven decision making. She explained technical and business trade-offs naturally with real examples from production environments, and her experience aligns well with the team’s authorization optimization and global expansion goals.\nNext steps would be to move her to the next round focused on deeper product strategy, payment optimization use cases, and cross-functional execution scenarios with additional stakeholders from the product and engineering leadership teams.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-28 20:45:04', '2026-05-28 20:45:04'),
(206, 492, 0, 'Final', 'Amazon', 'RAM', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Aritra presented strong system design and platform-thinking skills throughout the interview. He effectively discussed onboarding strategies, payment platform abstractions, configuration-driven design, and was receptive to feedback, continuously refining his design based on new requirements. In the middle of the interview, there were some internet connectivity issues; however, Aritra handled the situation calmly and professionally without losing the context of the discussion.\nHe showed good communication skills, collaborated well with the interviewer, and was able to reason through trade-offs between hosted pages, SDKs, APIs, and platform ownership models. While there were moments where he initially focused on implementation details before fully understanding the broader platform requirements, he adapted quickly and incorporated feedback effectively, demonstrating strong problem-solving ability and a growth mindset. Overall, he performed well and showed solid potential for a platform-focused software engineering role', '', 4.00, '2026-05-28 23:20:22', '2026-05-28 23:20:22'),
(207, 498, 0, 'NA', 'NA', 'NA', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'the candidate has to gone throw the RUC doc', 'NA', 1.00, '2026-05-29 13:46:06', '2026-05-29 13:46:06'),
(208, 499, 0, 'NA', 'NA', 'NA', 5, 5, 5, 5, 'Yes', 'the candidate has to gone throw the RUC doc wich is provided', 'NA', 5.00, '2026-05-29 13:47:09', '2026-05-29 13:47:09'),
(209, 420, 0, '1st', 'Deloitte', 'Budzik. Jackie', 3, 2, 3, 2, 'Yes', 'The candidate’s interview performance was average. She appeared nervous while responding to questions and struggled with brief pauses of 4–5 seconds, which gave an impression of limited technical knowledge. However, once provided with the answers, she was able to answer naturally and effectively.\nEnhancing her understanding of the technical concepts listed on her resume and building greater confidence during interviews would likely improve her chances of selection.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQDrqLqY9KeJR6QY2A0t17EcAZiaDaFE7Fr-a5HiUHPk-A8?e=PokzFi&nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJTdHJlYW1XZWJBcHAiLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJTaGFyZURpYWxvZy1MaW5rIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXcifX0%3D', 2.50, '2026-05-29 14:57:47', '2026-05-29 14:57:47'),
(210, 485, 0, '1st', 'Polestar Analytics', 'Aditya Majumder', 4, 4, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The interview went well overall. The candidate has shown significant improvement based on previous mistakes and past experience. He was able to answer the questions; however, the responses were not fully aligned with the interviewer’s expectations, particularly in terms of including specific keywords and providing more precise answers.\nAdditionally, he frequently repeated or reconfirmed questions before answering, which created an impression of uncertainty and may have negatively impacted the interviewer’s overall assessment.\nHis communication skills were good overall. A slight improvement in confidence while answering questions would further enhance his interview performance.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQC7icsv8unQQIURdlH5teRjAZI2CTT804Hbs4LDt4oZ3-U?e=nCYkrs&nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJTdHJlYW1XZWJBcHAiLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJTaGFyZURpYWxvZy1MaW5rIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXcifX0%3D', 3.50, '2026-05-29 15:09:43', '2026-05-29 15:09:43'),
(211, 481, 0, 'N/A', 'GMass', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Cancelled', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQCxLlfcCsRNTJfD4I6CzmPgAW07TTrIQXCycv2ScUPc97s?e=8cAsle&nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJTdHJlYW1XZWJBcHAiLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJTaGFyZURpYWxvZy1MaW5rIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXcifX0%3D', 1.00, '2026-05-29 15:12:00', '2026-05-29 15:12:00'),
(212, 473, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'RUC has been completed and document is shared', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-05-29 15:12:40', '2026-05-29 15:12:40'),
(213, 502, 0, '1st - phone call', 'HW3', 'Emma', 4, 2, 3, 2, 'Yes', 'The interview was conducted over a phone call, and despite occasional voice disruptions from the interviewer’s side, the candidate handled the situation well.\nIt appeared that the candidate was not fully confident with some of the technical concepts mentioned in the resume. During technical discussions, he seemed slightly nervous and occasionally reconfirmed questions before answering, possibly to cover gaps in understanding. However, once guided, he was able to respond naturally and communicate his answers clearly.\nHis communication skills were good overall, and the interviewer appreciated his openness and willingness to elaborate further during the discussion. The interviewer also mentioned that, even if this particular role does not work out, there may be other opportunities in the future that align with his profile. Additionally, the interviewer stated that they would reach out regarding the next round.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQC0-osqCQehTpCpD2SuRbj1AZ7hUNLHTZuJVEGdt0sjTww?e=ApaLi4&nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJTdHJlYW1XZWJBcHAiLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJTaGFyZURpYWxvZy1MaW5rIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXcifX0%3D', 2.75, '2026-05-29 15:33:46', '2026-05-29 15:33:46'),
(214, 509, 0, '2', 'Syntax Data', 'Jesse', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Dhruvil presented strong backend engineering fundamentals with solid knowledge of distributed systems, API design, caching, and problem-solving. He communicated his thought process clearly, showed good ownership of his projects, and handled follow-up design questions around LRU cache and TTL extensions well while also displaying strong collaboration and mentorship qualities.\n\nNext Steps: Proceed to the Hiring Manager round to further evaluate system design depth, stakeholder management, cross-functional collaboration, and ability to work with financial/business teams. Based on today\'s discussion, the candidate appears to be a strong fit for continued consideration in the interview process.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-29 16:19:58', '2026-05-29 16:19:58'),
(215, 525, 0, 'TAC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'It was a red planet assessment. Which was completed successfully passing both the test cases.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-29 16:21:19', '2026-05-29 16:21:19'),
(216, 514, 0, '1st Round', 'Wells (Motion Recruitment)', 'Mahesh Deshmukh', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'Even after 50+ interviews, placement would be difficult at the current level. Needs extensive mock interview practice and significant improvement in explaining concepts clearly, handling follow-up questions, project discussions, and overall confidence during interviews. Technical fundamentals are weak, and answers often lack practical understanding and depth.', '', 1.00, '2026-05-29 19:09:14', '2026-05-29 19:09:14'),
(217, 511, 0, 'Second Round (GenAI & Agentic Systems)', 'EXL', 'Kunal Patil', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'Strong understanding of Agentic RAG, LangGraph, LangSmith, multi-agent workflows, and overall GenAI concepts. Explained Allianz project well and handled follow-up questions honestly. Need deeper hands-on knowledge of GraphRAG, vector database internals, embedding strategies for multimodal data, and GCP services. Could improve system design discussions by focusing more on architectural decision-making rather than listing multiple solutions. Coding performance was good for basic problems but can improve on optimization-focused and follow-up scenarios.', '', 3.00, '2026-05-29 19:09:46', '2026-05-29 19:09:46'),
(218, 512, 0, '2', 'Microsoft', 'Rey', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well.Priyanshi demonstrated strong project management fundamentals and communicated her experience clearly with real-world examples from Walmart and HUL. She showed good stakeholder management, project execution, problem-solving, and process improvement capabilities while maintaining a professional and collaborative approach throughout the discussion.\n\nNext Steps: Candidate successfully completed the interview round and will move into the final feedback review process with the interview panel. The hiring team will consolidate interviewer feedback and determine next steps within the next 1-2 weeks.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-29 20:12:07', '2026-05-29 20:12:07'),
(219, 513, 0, '3', 'Microsoft', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well.Priyanshi displayed a strong understanding of the Data Center Project Manager role and effectively connected her previous project management experience to Microsoft\'s operational environment. She showed enthusiasm for the role, openness to relocation, strong communication skills, and a practical mindset around operations, process improvement, and cross-functional collaboration.\n\nNext Steps: All interview rounds have been completed. Interviewers will submit their evaluations and participate in a debrief discussion with the recruiting team. Following the review of all candidates, the recruiter will communicate the final hiring decision and any subsequent steps in the process.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-29 20:12:49', '2026-05-29 20:12:49'),
(220, 529, 0, '1', 'Addison', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. James presented good communication skills, professionalism, and a positive attitude throughout the interview. He showed a growth-oriented mindset, was receptive to learning new skills, and effectively highlighted his transferable experience in leadership, teamwork, and stakeholder coordination.\nNext Steps: The candidate will be reviewed alongside other second-round applicants by the hiring team. If selected to move forward, he will be contacted regarding the next stage of the process, which will include an orientation discussion and confirmation of start date availability.', '', 4.00, '2026-05-29 20:13:37', '2026-05-29 20:13:37'),
(221, 526, 0, 'NA', 'NA', 'NA', 4, 4, 5, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Lokesh was able to effectively connect his experience with multi-agent systems, RAG, and workflow-driven AI platforms to the real-world problems discussed during the conversation. He demonstrated a solid understanding of building practical AI solutions, translating business requirements into technical designs, and balancing quick MVP delivery with long-term scalable platform development. Overall, his responses were relevant, thoughtful, and aligned well with the expectations of the role.', '', 4.25, '2026-05-29 20:24:06', '2026-05-29 20:24:06'),
(222, 535, 0, 'NA', 'Keystone', 'NA', 4, 4, 5, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Lokesh was able to effectively connect his experience with multi-agent systems, RAG, and workflow-driven AI platforms to the real-world problems discussed during the conversation. He showed a solid understanding of building practical AI solutions, translating business requirements into technical designs, and balancing quick MVP delivery with long-term scalable platform development. Overall, his responses were relevant, thoughtful, and aligned well with the expectations of the role.', '', 4.25, '2026-05-29 20:29:44', '2026-05-29 20:29:44'),
