(255, 542, 0, 'Screening Round', 'HSB', 'Debbie', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. It was a screening round. She showed FP&A fundamentals with hands-on experience in budgeting, forecasting, variance analysis, management reporting, Power BI, SQL, and reporting automation. She communicated clearly, showed good business partnering experience, and aligned well with the reporting transformation and analytics aspects of the role, although her overall experience is slightly below the 7+ years preferred in the JD.\n\nNext Steps: Recommend moving forward to the hiring manager interview round for a deeper assessment of her FP&A expertise, Power BI capabilities, financial systems knowledge, and ability to lead reporting and process improvement initiatives within the finance organization.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-01 18:51:38', '2026-06-01 18:51:38'),
(256, 543, 0, '1st Round Technical Screening (Coding + Backend + ', 'Tesla', 'Calvin Wang', 3, 1, 3, 1, 'Yes', 'Candidate communicated his thought process clearly and asked relevant clarifying questions throughout the discussion. During the coding exercise, he explained the approach before implementation, but the final solution did not produce the expected output. The interviewer specifically mentioned that the implementation was still far from a working result and expected the candidate to first solve the given example correctly before discussing thresholds, edge cases, or further enhancements. Candidate should focus on validating the output against the requirement and delivering a working solution before moving to optimizations.', '', 2.00, '2026-06-01 19:13:51', '2026-06-01 19:13:51'),
