(269, 540, 0, '2', 'Davita', 'NO', 3, 3, 3, 2, 'Yes', 'She explained most of the topics well. However, in some cases, she did not refer to the documentation, which caused a few important points to be missed. As a result, some of her strategic answers lacked completeness when she responded to the interviewer.', '', 2.75, '2026-06-02 14:41:22', '2026-06-02 14:41:22'),
(270, 549, 0, 'Screening', 'Dexian', 'Parth', 2, 2, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Arohi presented Business Analysis fundamentals, particularly in requirements gathering, stakeholder management, SQL-based data analysis, API integrations, and Agile delivery. She answered questions and provided relevant project examples; however, she can further improve by speaking more clearly, slowing down her pace, and articulating certain technical concepts and domain-specific terms more precisely.\nNext Steps: Proceed with the hiring manager round. Prior to the interview, it would be beneficial for her to strengthen her knowledge of investment data, investment workflows, and common investment technology platforms such as Aladdin, while continuing to improve verbal communication and answer delivery for a more polished presentation.', '', 2.00, '2026-06-02 14:52:30', '2026-06-02 14:52:30'),
(271, 557, 0, '', 'DSM-H Consulting', 'Thomas Williams', 3, 3, 3, 2, 'Yes', 'Need to improve confidence while answering technical questions and avoid giving lengthy explanations for straightforward questions. Should focus on providing more project-specific examples when discussing API automation frameworks, Java programming, and testing strategies. Also needs to ask clarifying questions before jumping into coding solutions and communicate the thought process more clearly during problem-solving.', '', 2.75, '2026-06-02 17:33:10', '2026-06-02 17:33:10'),
(272, 556, 0, 'Screening Round', 'RadixArk', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Prateek showed good communication skills, structured product thinking, and a solid understanding of customer discovery, roadmap prioritization, and cross-functional collaboration. While his AI infrastructure knowledge is still developing, he showed genuine curiosity, learned quickly during the discussion, and was able to connect product decisions with customer and business impact effectively.\n\nNext Steps: Move forward to the next interview stage focused on product case studies and problem-solving. Further evaluation should assess his ability to prioritize roadmap investments, handle open-source product strategy, analyze customer feedback at scale, and make data-driven decisions in an AI infrastructure environment.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-02 18:08:07', '2026-06-02 18:08:07'),
