(289, 573, 0, 'Screening', 'BNI', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Gauri showed strong FP&A fundamentals, particularly in forecasting, budgeting, variance analysis, reporting, and business partnering. She communicated clearly, showed a genuine interest in helping build a more strategic finance organization, and her experience with financial systems, Power BI, Adaptive Planning, and process improvement appears to align well with the team\'s current needs.\n\nNext Steps:\n\nWe will be moving Gauri forward to the next round. The next interview will be a technical working session focused on an Excel-based business case designed to simulate the type of financial analysis performed within the team. Following that, successful candidates will participate in a final panel interview with the CFO and other key finance stakeholders.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-03 15:42:22', '2026-06-03 15:42:22'),
(290, 575, 0, 'Technical Round 1', 'Infosys (Client: Citi Bank)', 'NA', 2, 1, 2, 1, 'Yes', 'Needs significant improvement in Java fundamentals, Collections Framework, HashMap internals, Comparable vs Comparator, SOLID principles, Spring Boot concepts, API security, API versioning, and rate limiting. Struggled with Microservices architecture, design patterns, CAP theorem, Docker, Cloud concepts, Angular fundamentals, and coding with Java Streams. Should focus on understanding core concepts and explaining them with practical examples and real-time implementation details.', '', 1.50, '2026-06-03 16:13:17', '2026-06-03 16:13:17'),
(291, 574, 0, '1st Round', 'Barclay', '--', 2, 2, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'The interview went okay. The interviewer asked several project-based questions, and we helped the candidate with answers for each of the question. However, while delivering the answers, the candidate was unable to explain them confidently and clearly. He appeared nervous, and at times it seemed as though he was reading the answers from somewhere rather than speaking naturally from his own understanding.', '--', 1.50, '2026-06-03 17:13:28', '2026-06-03 17:13:28'),
(292, 572, 0, 'Final', 'E-Solutions Inc (UST)', 'John', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Hemachandra presented experience in Azure-based data engineering, data quality management, stakeholder communication, and production support. He was able to explain his project experience, root cause analysis approach, and collaboration with business teams clearly, though deeper technical probing around Spark performance tuning, SQL optimization, and Databricks internals may be beneficial in future discussions.\nNext Steps:\nProceed to the next round for further evaluation of hands-on technical depth in Spark, Databricks, Snowflake, and large-scale data processing, while considering him a strong fit from a communication, ownership, and stakeholder management perspective.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-03 20:34:37', '2026-06-03 20:34:37'),
(293, 570, 0, 'Screening', 'TCS', 'N/A', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'Interview went fair. He presented good knowledge of Python fundamentals and was able to understand the problem, explain the approach, discuss time and space complexity, and develop a logical solution without relying on built-in functions. Communication was clear, and the candidate showed a structured problem-solving approach throughout the discussion.\n\nDuring the coding exercise, the online IDE provided by the interviewer appeared to have execution or environment-related issues, which impacted code validation and output verification. Despite this, the candidate was able to explain the expected behavior of the solution, debug systematically, and articulate the reasoning behind the implementation.', '', 3.00, '2026-06-03 20:38:12', '2026-06-03 20:38:12'),
