(305, 590, 0, '3rd Technical', 'Aera Technology', 'N/A', 3, 4, 3, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Neema presented solid knowledge of Kubernetes, Terraform, Linux, networking, and production troubleshooting concepts. She was able to answer most questions correctly and showed a good understanding of real-world infrastructure and platform engineering practices, though at times she appeared hesitant and could have communicated her answers with greater confidence and ownership.\n\nNext Steps:\n\nThe technical feedback will be reviewed internally by the engineering team. If selected, the candidate will proceed to the final interview round with senior leadership (VP/CEO level), which will focus more on communication, architectural thinking, problem-solving approach, and overall fit for the role. Improving confidence, reducing pauses, and delivering answers more assertively would significantly strengthen her performance in future rounds.', '', 3.50, '2026-06-04 13:37:59', '2026-06-04 13:37:59'),
(306, 571, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'We have successfully completed his second training session. During this session, we covered virtual environments, including their purpose and the process of activating them. Following the training, we provided hands-on coding exercises to be completed during the session and assigned additional coding tasks as take-home practice to reinforce the concepts learned.', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-04 13:40:07', '2026-06-04 13:40:07'),
(307, 592, 0, 'Screening', 'Mercy Health', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'Interview did not start. She attempted to join the interview, but the meeting link downloaded a Screen Connect installer instead of opening Zoom Meet. Before installing any software, she wanted to confirm whether this was intentional and request an alternate meeting link.\n\nThe installer named \"unauthorised publisher\" is actually trying to install Atera Agent. Atera is a Screen connect tool used by IT teams, but it is not Zoom Meet.', '', 1.00, '2026-06-04 16:20:58', '2026-06-04 16:20:58'),
(308, 604, 0, 'Final', 'WSP', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Gauri presented strong financial analysis, forecasting, reporting, and stakeholder management skills throughout the discussion. While she lacks direct bridge inspection and DOT industry experience, she communicated well, showed a growth mindset, and aligned strongly with the VP\'s expectations around ownership, accountability, transparency, and long-term commitment.\n\nNext Steps:\n\nProceed to the next stage and consider extending an offer in the $90K range with H1B sponsorship support. Candidate should be evaluated on her ability to quickly learn the infrastructure domain but overall appears to be a strong fit for a high-ownership Business/Financial Analyst role supporting regional leadership and strategic decision-making.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-04 16:34:48', '2026-06-04 16:34:48'),
