(313, 608, 0, '1st', 'Red Hat', 'Jay Koehler, Tramaine Darby', 3, 2, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'Manushree showed significant improvement in communication compared to her previous interviews. She handled follow-up questions confidently, maintained good conversation flow, and explained her experience in a natural way. She was able to justify project decisions and discuss AI, architecture, and team collaboration effectively. Going forward, she can further strengthen the depth of some project metrics and provide more specific examples when discussing business impact and technical ownership. Overall, this was one of her stronger interview performances.', '', 2.25, '2026-06-04 19:55:48', '2026-06-04 19:55:48'),
(314, 612, 0, 'First', 'Truth Initiative', 'N/A', 3, 4, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Liza showed analytical thinking, solid experience in marketing analytics, campaign performance measurement, SQL, dashboarding, and cross-functional collaboration. She provided relevant examples from her experience and did a good job connecting business problems to data-driven recommendations, which aligned well with the role\'s requirements.\n\nNext Steps: The candidate will move into the evaluation pool as the team continues completing first-round interviews. The hiring team will review all candidates and determine who will advance to the next stage of the process.\n\nArea for Improvement: Liza would benefit from slowing down her responses slightly and speaking more clearly and deliberately. At times, her answers contained strong content, but a slower pace would make her communication more polished, easier to follow, and allow her insights to have a stronger impact during interviews.', '', 3.25, '2026-06-04 20:42:11', '2026-06-04 20:42:11'),
(315, 610, 0, 'Phone screening', 'Ford', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'Interview went OK. It was a phone screening meet. Kinesh showed background in Machine Learning Engineering with relevant experience in Python, cloud environments, production ML systems, and AI-related technologies. He was able to clearly explain his experience and showed good alignment with the role requirements, particularly around MLOps, ML deployment, and enterprise-scale AI solutions.\n\nCommunication was good overall, but he could improve by providing more structured and confident responses. At times, answers were slightly short and reactive. Adding more real project examples, speaking with greater conviction, and focusing on business impact would make his responses more compelling and memorable to hiring managers.\n\nAreas for Improvement\nSpeak more confidently and avoid sounding uncertain when discussing experience.\nExpand answers with specific examples from KeyBank and AT&T.\nFocus on outcomes and business impact, not just technologies used.\nWhen discussing newer technologies like LangChain or RAG, confidently explain practical exposure without underselling experience.\nSlow down slightly and organize responses into Problem → What I Did → Result.\nNext Steps\n\nThe recruiter will share the profile and interview notes with the Hiring Manager. If selected, the candidate will be invited to a 30-minute Hiring Manager interview focused on technical experience, AI/ML projects, cloud platforms, Python, RAG, LLMs, and production system design. Successful completion of that round will lead to a full interview loop conducted via Microsoft Teams. Overall recommendation: Proceed to Hiring Manager Round.', '', 1.00, '2026-06-04 21:17:25', '2026-06-04 21:17:25'),
(316, 569, 0, 'Screening Round', 'Amazon', '--', 3, 3, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'This is not the actual interview. In this meeting, the interviewer is only explaining all the details about the Amazon interview process. After this, they may schedule the actual interview for the candidate.', '--', 2.50, '2026-06-04 22:05:10', '2026-06-04 22:05:10'),
(317, 615, 0, 'NA', 'NA', 'NA', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'The candidate answered most questions correctly. However, she sometimes wrapped up answers too quickly without providing enough detail, and at times it seemed like she was referring to notes while answering. I suggested elaborating more on responses, maintaining better eye contact, and adjusting the camera setup. Overall, the interview performance was average', 'NA', 1.00, '2026-06-04 22:09:36', '2026-06-04 22:09:36'),
(318, 580, 0, 'Interview Round', 'Walmart', 'Nagappa Paraddi', 4, 4, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'This was the coding round of the interview. They asked two coding questions, and we helped the candidate solve both of them successfully. At the end of the interview, they mentioned that they would reach out regarding the next steps.', '--', 3.50, '2026-06-04 22:18:20', '2026-06-04 22:18:20'),
(319, 602, 0, '2nd', 'JPMorganChase', 'Lauren Goodwin', 4, 3, 4, 2, 'Yes', 'Interview went well, candidate was giving answers perfectly and was able to handle the gap. overall, we can say that candidate might be selected for the next round based on the conversation.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQDlEKuWAifHRLJZ0qS4ZWz0AY-3N7wvMP7a7j2Zy-z9jB8?nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJPbmVEcml2ZUZvckJ1c2luZXNzIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXciLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJNeUZpbGVzTGlua0NvcHkifX0&e=tYQd8Q', 3.25, '2026-06-04 22:18:59', '2026-06-04 22:18:59'),
(320, 613, 0, 'Behavioral Round', 'Phenom', 'Kaushik Siddharth, Bishal Baisak', 4, 4, 4, 3, 'Yes', 'The interview went well in this round. The interviewer asked project-based and scenario-based questions, and we helped the candidate with each answer. The candidate was able to respond accurately and confidently. At the end, they mentioned that they will reach out regarding the next step in the interview process.', '--', 3.75, '2026-06-04 22:27:40', '2026-06-04 22:27:40'),
(321, 586, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'It was a mock session, and it has been completed successfully.', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-05 13:21:27', '2026-06-05 13:21:27'),
(322, 585, 0, 'RUC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'RUC is completed and its done', '', 1.00, '2026-06-05 14:35:34', '2026-06-05 14:35:34'),
(323, 595, 0, '3rd', 'Integra connect', 'Alex Persechino, Bryan Walton.', 4, 3, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'The interview went well overall. The interviewer asked a combination of scenario-based and technical questions, and the candidate provided accurate and appropriate responses throughout. We also provided guidance during the interview on how to structure and present the answers more effectively.\nHowever, the candidate appeared panicked and nervous at certain points during the discussion, which was also noticed by the interviewer. In fact, the interviewer reassured the candidate by mentioning that there was no need to be nervous or panic. The candidate particularly struggled at times to maintain the gap between the questions asked and the responses given in the provided document, which contributed to the nervousness during those moments.\nAt the conclusion of the interview, the interviewer expressed satisfaction with the candidate’s responses and specifically mentioned that the candidate handled the discussion well.\nOverall, based on the quality of the answers provided, we can say that the candidate is likely to move forward to the next round', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQD0pU5T4K2hTL8_u_RRH40xAQxbTgaq4e1TRweEmpe8pMw?e=ugnTu0&nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJTdHJlYW1XZWJBcHAiLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJTaGFyZURpYWxvZy1MaW5rIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXcifX0%3D', 3.75, '2026-06-05 14:49:15', '2026-06-05 14:49:15'),
(324, 599, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', '3rd session has been completed', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-05 14:51:26', '2026-06-05 14:51:26'),
(325, 587, 0, 'TAC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'TAC is completed easily', '', 1.00, '2026-06-05 15:16:40', '2026-06-05 15:16:40'),
(326, 630, 0, 'Screening', 'Slalom', 'N/A', 3, 3, 4, 3, 'Yes', 'Interview went fair. He presented good alignment with the Cyber Security Engineer role, showcasing solid experience in AWS security, DevSecOps, application security, SAST tools, security automation, and containerized environments. He communicated his experience clearly, provided relevant real-world examples, and showed a good understanding of secure development and cloud security practices.\nNext Steps: Move the candidate forward to the Slalom technical interview for a deeper assessment of AWS security, Terraform, DevSecOps, application security, and automation capabilities. If the technical round is successful, proceed with client submission and final interview consideration.', '', 3.25, '2026-06-05 18:37:13', '2026-06-05 18:37:13'),
(327, 617, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', '3rd training session has been completed successfully', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-05 18:38:01', '2026-06-05 18:38:01'),
(328, 639, 0, 'Final', 'Trantor', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. She presented strong communication skills and a unique combination of FP&A domain expertise, Workday Adaptive Planning experience, and Agentic AI knowledge. She was transparent about areas outside her direct experience, showed solid problem-solving ability, and aligned well with the organization\'s vision of transforming finance processes through automation and AI.\n\nNext Steps: Proceed with the next round involving Finance Leadership or key business stakeholders to further evaluate her understanding of finance operations, process transformation capabilities, and ability to collaborate across finance and technology teams on enterprise-wide AI initiatives.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-05 18:38:14', '2026-06-05 18:38:14'),
(329, 644, 0, '2 Technical', 'THRIFTBOOK', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Gauri presented strong communication skills, business acumen, and a solid blend of financial and technical expertise throughout the discussion. She effectively articulated her experience in FP&A, forecasting, automation, and cross-functional collaboration, while also showing curiosity, ownership, and a genuine interest in understanding the business beyond the numbers.\n\nNext Steps: Candidate will proceed to the next stage of the interview process for further evaluation with the leadership team. Based on today\'s discussion, she appears to be a strong fit for an environment that values business partnership, data-driven decision making, and operational finance.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-05 18:47:40', '2026-06-05 18:47:40'),
(330, 642, 0, 'NA', 'NA', 'NA', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'He\'s an experienced candidate, so explained him easily', 'NA', 1.00, '2026-06-05 18:48:24', '2026-06-05 18:48:24'),
(331, 638, 0, '1st', 'EXL', 'Tanu Mittal', 3, 2, 3, 2, 'Yes', 'The interview was average. It was looking like he was reading from somewhere and also before start of the interview the support person mentioned that while the support person is writing the code the candidate should explain the code when it is written but he was just sitting and was explaining nothing when support person was writing. And also, he needs a strong improvement is commination skills like speaking, he was constantly speaking without any pauses.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQAI_a43RNlSTYhzOkz9y6XTAalLO737zRtGoZrRBYoVmzk?nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJPbmVEcml2ZUZvckJ1c2luZXNzIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXciLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJNeUZpbGVzTGlua0NvcHkifX0&e=yY7iAO', 2.50, '2026-06-05 18:49:37', '2026-06-05 18:49:37'),
(332, 632, 0, 'Technical Round', 'Discounttire', 'Carrie McElhaney, Pranay Reddy, Alma Salcido, Gautam Reddy', 2, 1, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'This was a panel interview where the interviewers shared their screen and asked the candidate to perform a live Workday configuration exercise. We provided guidance throughout the exercise; however, the candidate was not able to clearly explain the steps being performed or the reasoning behind the configuration decisions.\n \nAnd from the candidate side, there were audio issues, making it difficult to clearly hear both the interviewers\' questions and the candidate\'s responses. Due to the lack of clear communication and limited understanding of the instructions being given during the exercise, the interaction was not very effective. The interview concluded shortly afterward.', '--', 1.25, '2026-06-05 18:57:17', '2026-06-05 18:57:17'),
(333, 631, 0, '1st Round.', 'WS Development', 'Reichlen, Jeff', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The interview went well. The interviewer asked several questions related to the project, and we assisted the candidate with the answers to each question. The candidate was able to respond accurately and confidently throughout the interview.', '--', 3.00, '2026-06-05 18:59:30', '2026-06-05 18:59:30'),
(334, 626, 0, '1st Round', 'WS Development', 'Reichlen, Jeff', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The interview went well. The interviewer asked several questions related to the project, and we assisted the candidate with the answers to each question. The candidate was able to respond accurately and confidently throughout the interview.', '--', 3.00, '2026-06-05 19:00:32', '2026-06-05 19:00:32'),
(335, 609, 0, '1st Round', 'ISI Enterprises', '--', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'During the interview, the candidate faced issues with their laptop as well as network connectivity problems. Due to these technical difficulties, the interviewer was unable to proceed with the interview.', '--', 1.00, '2026-06-05 19:04:10', '2026-06-05 19:04:10'),
(336, 593, 0, 'Technical Round', 'env.nm.gov', '--', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The interview went good. At the beginning, the interviewer mentioned that they would ask only 11 questions, and they asked exactly 11 questions during the interview. We assisted the candidate with answers to each question, and the candidate was able to respond accurately and confidently. At the end of the interview, the interviewer mentioned that they would reach out regarding the next steps in the interview process.', '--', 3.00, '2026-06-05 19:08:03', '2026-06-05 19:08:03'),
(337, 619, 0, 'Coding Round', 'Apple', '--', 2, 2, 2, 2, 'No', 'The interview went okay. The interviewer asked project-based and technical questions. After that, the interviewer asked one coding question. We helped the candidate with the answers to each question, but the candidate was not able to provide proper responses. We also helped the candidate solve the coding problem.', '--', 2.00, '2026-06-05 19:13:47', '2026-06-05 19:13:47'),
(338, 621, 0, 'Technical', 'Infosys', 'N/A', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'Interview went ok. Mayur presented experience in AI/ML concepts, RAG pipelines, prompt engineering, Python, and data engineering fundamentals. He communicated his project experience well; however, the interview was impacted by extensive cross-questioning and frequent requirement changes by the Indian interviewer which made it difficult to fully showcase his technical depth and problem-solving approach.\nNext Steps:\nProceed with an internal review of the interview feedback and technical assessment. If shortlisted, schedule the next round focusing on hands-on AI/ML, RAG architecture, Python development, and real-world system design discussions to better evaluate his practical experience and technical capabilities.', '', 3.00, '2026-06-05 21:37:02', '2026-06-05 21:37:02'),
(339, 622, 0, 'Technical', 'Infosys', 'N/A', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'Interview went ok. Mayur presented understanding of AI/ML concepts, RAG architectures, embeddings, AWS services, and overall cloud-based AI solutions. However, there were noticeable gaps in Python fundamentals, Fast API implementation, authentication concepts, and SQL query writing, which are critical for enterprise-level development roles. During the discussion, the interviewer unexpectedly left the meeting midway without informing the candidate and later rejoined, after which the interview continued normally.\nNext Steps:\nThe candidate may be considered for further evaluation based on project requirements. It is recommended that Mayur strengthen Python programming, Fast API, database concepts, SQL querying, and backend development fundamentals while continuing to build expertise in AI/ML technologies. A final decision will be shared after internal feedback review and discussion with the hiring team', '', 3.00, '2026-06-05 21:37:51', '2026-06-05 21:37:51'),
(340, 651, 0, '1st', 'Colgate', 'Chris Frank', 4, 4, 3, 4, 'Yes', 'Candidate was confident and gave answers effectively. He demonstrated strong communication and technical skills and had also done research on both the JD and the interviewer. The interviewer appeared satisfied with his responses, and the candidate was capable of handling gaps in the conversation smoothly and mostly he will be move forward with the next round.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQAmplgAznASQ4BrOZ2OvziJAYsj3NTJ3X9CEnzBLHuikeo?e=aNKlQN&nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJTdHJlYW1XZWJBcHAiLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJTaGFyZURpYWxvZy1MaW5rIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXcifX0%3D', 3.75, '2026-06-08 15:57:52', '2026-06-08 15:57:52'),
(341, 650, 0, '1', 'Orrick', 'No', 2, 2, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'It was just a screening round. The candidate appeared to be referring to answers during the interview, and it looked like he was reading them rather than responding naturally.\n\nWe provided feedback that he should avoid sitting idle during pauses. There were noticeable gaps where he remained silent, and then suddenly started explaining once he seemed to find the answer. This created the impression that he was looking up or reading responses instead of answering based on his own knowledge.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQAh14Ag27lWRIlGspM0g-7sAcpfc2jV9nFbwtgTOuTkxBU?nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJPbmVEcml2ZUZvckJ1c2luZXNzIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXciLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJNeUZpbGVzTGlua0NvcHkifX0&e=Pwy2N0', 2.00, '2026-06-08 16:06:26', '2026-06-08 16:06:26');
