(359, 628, 0, 'Interview (1 Round) screening Call', 'EXL SERVICES', 'NA', 2, 2, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'Need to go with the basics thinks', '', 2.00, '2026-06-08 20:29:19', '2026-06-08 20:29:19'),
(360, 652, 0, 'Screening', 'Quanata', 'Vijay, Tim, Prashanth', 2, 2, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'There was a miscommunication between the candidate and recruiter regarding the expectation of a PPT presentation on a recent testing-focused project. Candidate attended without a prepared presentation.\nInterviewers were expecting a structured walkthrough of a recent project with emphasis on testing strategy, quality ownership, validations, defects, automation, and business impact.\nCandidate explained high-level concepts around Kafka, data pipelines, and data quality but struggled when interviewers asked deeper questions around real-world testing scenarios and ownership.\nSeveral examples became theoretical instead of being backed by actual project experience.\nNeed stronger preparation around discussing testing activities, validation strategies, regression testing, API testing, data quality checks, and production monitoring using concrete examples from recent projects.\nOverall interview performance was below average, and I am not confident about the chances of moving forward to the next round.', '', 1.50, '2026-06-08 20:30:20', '2026-06-08 20:30:20'),
(361, 661, 0, 'Screening / Initial Round', 'Waste Management', 'NA', 2, 1, 2, 1, 'Yes', 'Need more improvement when delivering the answers', '', 1.50, '2026-06-08 20:32:23', '2026-06-08 20:32:23'),
(362, 654, 0, '1', 'NA', 'NA', 2, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'The interview went well overall. The interviewer explained the coding problem, discussed the expected approach, and reviewed the optimal solution strategy. I successfully implemented the solution, and all test cases passed without any issues.', '', 3.50, '2026-06-08 21:18:45', '2026-06-08 21:18:45'),
(363, 655, 0, '2', 'NA', 'NA', 4, 4, 4, 1, 'Yes', 'The interview went well overall. The interviewer explained the system design problem in detail and discussed the key requirements, architectural considerations, and design trade-offs involved. We had a productive discussion on the proposed design approach, scalability, performance, and component interactions, which helped me effectively communicate my thought process and solution.', '', 3.25, '2026-06-08 21:20:14', '2026-06-08 21:20:14'),
(364, 635, 0, 'NA', 'NA', 'NA', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Cancelled', '', 1.00, '2026-06-08 21:25:17', '2026-06-08 21:25:17'),
(365, 634, 0, 'TAC', 'NA', 'NA', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'All test cases -> Success', '', 1.00, '2026-06-08 21:26:49', '2026-06-08 21:26:49'),
(366, 577, 0, 'JDC', 'NA', 'NA', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Good Candidate', '', 1.00, '2026-06-08 21:27:42', '2026-06-08 21:27:42'),
(367, 658, 0, 'Technical', 'JBS', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. She presented a good understanding of SAP MM fundamentals, including Procure-to-Pay, material master, purchasing organization structure, release strategies, MRP, reorder points, and procurement processes. Communication was clear and professional throughout the interview, and she showed a willingness to learn while effectively relating technical concepts to business processes.\nNext Steps: The interview panel will complete internal discussions and compare feedback with other candidates. Sierra from HR will reach out regarding the outcome of the interview and communicate any next steps in the hiring process.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-08 21:33:18', '2026-06-08 21:33:18'),
(368, 667, 0, 'RUC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'RUC Completed.', '', 1.00, '2026-06-08 21:33:40', '2026-06-08 21:33:40'),
(369, 643, 0, 'na', 'na', 'na', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'explained RUC, candidate said she\'ll go through the document and if have any doubts she\'ll contact', 'na', 1.00, '2026-06-09 14:15:49', '2026-06-09 14:15:49'),
(370, 624, 0, '1st', 'Internet Brands', 'Jay Masilamani', 4, 4, 3, 3, 'No', 'The interview went well. The candidate answered the questions accurately, and the communication skills were good. The interviewer asked several cross-questions, all of which were answered effectively, and the interviewer appeared satisfied with the responses.\nA slight improvement in energy levels, hand gestures, and facial expressions would further enhance the overall quality of the interview.\nThe candidate was using his own AI tool for generating answers and had informed us before the start of the interview that he would be using AI-generated responses instead of the answers provided in our document.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQDIf5QpQXolTqS7t_LvaLTlAZS_jqKmgPwAHEDFWSLu93M?e=cGx8oL&nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJTdHJlYW1XZWJBcHAiLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJTaGFyZURpYWxvZy1MaW5rIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXcifX0%3D', 3.50, '2026-06-09 14:50:43', '2026-06-09 14:50:43'),
(371, 647, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Ruc session has been completed but candidate has doubts which were from resume and so he said he will change the details and will connect again', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-09 14:55:19', '2026-06-09 14:55:19'),
(372, 668, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Ruc session has been completed, and candidate has doubts regarding the projects, she didn\'t need whole ruc session just she had doubts which we solved, and she was satisfied with the answers.', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-09 15:01:48', '2026-06-09 15:01:48'),
(373, 671, 0, 'Screening', 'BMO', 'N/A', 2, 2, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'Interview went ok. Arohi has required background in Business Analysis, documentation, governance, and traceability, and she was able to explain her experience with relevant examples from the banking domain. Going forward, she should focus on keeping the interview more conversational, speaking clearly and confidently, and providing specific project-based examples with more detail to strengthen her responses and create a stronger connection with the interviewer.', '', 2.00, '2026-06-09 15:29:59', '2026-06-09 15:29:59'),
(374, 674, 0, 'Final', 'Pepsico', 'Christopher', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. She presented good understanding of SAP S/4HANA supply chain and warehouse-related processes, communicated clearly throughout the discussion, and showed strong willingness to travel and support field operations during deployment and Hypercare activities. While direct Blue Yonder experience is limited, she effectively positioned her SAP warehouse, inventory management, and end-user support background as transferable skills and appeared capable of ramping up quickly within the team\'s onboarding model.\n\nNext Steps:\n\nThe candidate will be reviewed alongside other applicants being interviewed this week. If selected to move forward, she can expect an update through the recruiting agency/portal within the next 1-2 business days regarding the next stage of the process, with onboarding targeted for June 21st pending successful completion of background screening and pre-employment requirements.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-09 17:49:01', '2026-06-09 17:49:01'),
(375, 673, 0, 'Technical Interview', 'Recogni', 'Yen Hsing Li', 3, 2, 3, 2, 'Yes', 'SystemVerilog, constraints, randomization, fork-join concepts, and basic verification methodology. She was able to solve most coding and constraint-based questions but required hints and follow-up guidance for some probability and constrained-randomization scenarios. Communication was clear overall, though answers could be more concise and confident in advanced SystemVerilog and solver-related topics. Candidate has a solid verification foundation and performed reasonably well throughout the discussion.', '', 2.50, '2026-06-09 18:20:15', '2026-06-09 18:20:15'),
(376, 636, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Ruc session has been completed, and candidate just need the doc he doesn\'t need the session, so document has been provided.', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-09 18:54:17', '2026-06-09 18:54:17'),
(377, 637, 0, 'RUC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'RUC session is completed \nthe candidate has a dought on the question section and wants a more most likely question from us', '', 1.00, '2026-06-09 19:41:03', '2026-06-09 19:41:03'),
(378, 640, 0, 'RUC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'CANCELLED', '', 1.00, '2026-06-09 19:41:32', '2026-06-09 19:41:32'),
(379, 669, 0, 'RUC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'RUC is completed', '', 1.00, '2026-06-09 19:41:57', '2026-06-09 19:41:57'),
(380, 666, 0, 'RUC', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'RUC  session is completed well', '', 1.00, '2026-06-09 19:42:22', '2026-06-09 19:42:22'),
(381, 682, 0, '2nd', 'RAZR', 'N/A', 2, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'Ebenezar presented, a collaborative mindset, and a mature approach to incident management, cross-functional teamwork, and continuous improvement. He provided practical examples from his experience, showed ownership of operational challenges, and aligned well with the team\'s culture of proactive problem-solving and knowledge sharing.\n\nNext Steps:\n\nThe candidate has successfully completed the architecture and culture-fit discussion. Proceed with the technical assignment review and consolidate feedback from Eugene, the Architecture team, and Engineering leadership before making a final hiring recommendation.', '', 2.75, '2026-06-09 20:07:30', '2026-06-09 20:07:30'),
(382, 675, 0, '3', 'upstart', 'NA', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'No', 'Overall good interview.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-09 20:34:08', '2026-06-09 20:34:08'),
(383, 683, 0, 'TAC', 'HackerRank', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'Yes', 'It was a hackerank assessment with three coding exercises in JAVA. All three questions were solved successfully, passing all the test and hidden edge cases.', '', 1.00, '2026-06-09 21:41:30', '2026-06-09 21:41:30'),
(384, 677, 0, 'N/A', 'RZR', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Interviewer did not show up.', '', 1.00, '2026-06-10 13:24:38', '2026-06-10 13:24:38'),
(385, 681, 0, 'TAC', 'Photon', '--', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', '--', '--', 1.00, '2026-06-10 13:32:12', '2026-06-10 13:32:12'),
(386, 672, 0, '1st Round', 'Genista Biosciences', 'Himani Sharma', 2, 2, 2, 2, 'Yes', 'The interview went okay. The interviewer asked general and experience-based questions. We helped the candidate with answers to each question, and the candidate responded accordingly. However, the candidate was not able to explain all of the responses accurately and needs to handle some seconds more independently during interviews. At the end of the interview, the interviewer mentioned that they would reach out regarding the next steps.', '--', 2.00, '2026-06-10 13:43:58', '2026-06-10 13:43:58'),
(387, 680, 0, '2nd Round.', 'Keystone', 'Alex', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The interview went well. The interviewer asked scenario-based questions, and we helped the candidate with answers to each question. The candidate was able to provide accurate responses and explain them effectively. At the end of the interview, the interviewer mentioned that they would reach out regarding the next steps. If the candidate is selected for the next round, it will be an onsite interview.', '--', 3.00, '2026-06-10 13:53:57', '2026-06-10 13:53:57'),
(388, 685, 0, '1st Round', 'EXL', 'Mohit Dhawan', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The interview went okay. The interviewer asked questions related to the candidate\'s project experience. We helped the candidate with answers to each question; however, the candidate did not accurately follow the guidance provided by the technical support person and instead gave their own responses. As a result, some of the answers were not technically accurate or complete. At the end of the interview, the interviewer mentioned that they would reach out regarding the next steps.', '--', 3.00, '2026-06-10 13:59:06', '2026-06-10 13:59:06'),
(389, 676, 0, '1st', 'ensemblehp', 'Servet Senlik', 3, 3, 4, 3, 'No', 'The interview was average overall. In the first half, which consisted of a rapid-fire round, the interviewer asked questions related to Python and Machine Learning, where the candidate demonstrated a satisfactory understanding. However, during the second half, which focused on code review and debugging, the candidate\'s performance was below expectations. The candidate relied on answers generated through their own AI tool rather than referring to the answers provided in our shared document. Additionally, the candidate generally provided short responses, whereas the interviewer expected more detailed and comprehensive explanations. Another concern is ensuring that the correct and updated resume is shared before scheduling interviews, as this issue occurred previously and was encountered again in this case. We are receiving he updated resume from the candidate. Furthermore, when advised to review the resume and strengthen the skills mentioned within resume, the candidate stated that he currently do not have sufficient time to learn new things.', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQDW1dfl5V_3T7cgHREXZte0AcC9ahtvAvWS3NdIMxBf_Os?nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJPbmVEcml2ZUZvckJ1c2luZXNzIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXciLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJNeUZpbGVzTGlua0NvcHkifX0&e=HUbiNk', 3.25, '2026-06-10 14:05:30', '2026-06-10 14:05:30'),
(390, 684, 0, 'N/A', 'N/A', 'N/A', 1, 1, 1, 1, 'No', 'Mock session has been completed successfully, and candidate has been explained how to be prepare for the interview. Additionally, Preparation material has been sent to the candidate.', 'N/A', 1.00, '2026-06-10 14:08:38', '2026-06-10 14:08:38'),
(391, 607, 0, '1', 'New Era Technology', 'NA', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'The Interview is completed Successfully the candidate shows his technical abilities but there is some points like confidence and the handling gap between questions  needs to work upon', 'https://infinitisyncglobal-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/bhadresh_bedgetechinc_com/IQBmVGPEQ0A4QJaFeowlQEOlAUyGX4Dn3K0l5yz52I3brew?nav=eyJyZWZlcnJhbEluZm8iOnsicmVmZXJyYWxBcHAiOiJPbmVEcml2ZUZvckJ1c2luZXNzIiwicmVmZXJyYWxBcHBQbGF0Zm9ybSI6IldlYiIsInJlZmVycmFsTW9kZSI6InZpZXciLCJyZWZlcnJhbFZpZXciOiJNeUZpbGVzTGlua0NvcHkifX0&e=H5IeuT', 3.00, '2026-06-10 15:34:05', '2026-06-10 15:34:05'),
(392, 688, 0, 'Final', 'Thriftbook', 'Kim', 3, 1, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. There was some technical issue within the laptop and end of the interview, But Gauri presented FP&A fundamentals with solid experience in forecasting, variance analysis, financial modeling, SQL, and executive reporting. She communicated clearly, provided relevant examples with measurable business impact, and showed a genuine interest in understanding the operational drivers behind the business rather than focusing solely on finance.\n\nNext Steps:\n\nThe candidate appears to be a strong fit from both a technical and behavioral perspective. Recommend advancing her to the next round with Finance leadership and key business stakeholders to further assess her ability to learn the business model, partner cross-functionally, and contribute to forecasting, profitability analysis, and strategic decision-making within the ThriftBooks environment.', '', 3.00, '2026-06-10 17:50:50', '2026-06-10 17:50:50'),
(393, 692, 0, '1 and 2', 'Wallmart', 'NA', 4, 4, 4, 5, 'Yes', 'Round 1 (Technical Round):\n\nThe interview went well. The candidate was presented with project-related bugs and missing code implementations to resolve. They successfully identified the issues, completed the required implementations, and ensured that all test cases passed. The candidate clearly explained their approach, reasoning, and code changes in a structured and effective manner, demonstrating strong problem-solving and debugging skills.\n\nRound 2 (Behavioral Round):\nThe candidate performed well in the behavioral round. They answered all questions confidently and provided clear, relevant, and well-structured responses. Their communication skills were strong, and they were able to articulate their thoughts and experiences effectively throughout the discussion.\n\nOverall Feedback:\nThe candidate Showed solid technical expertise, strong problem-solving abilities, and good coding practices. They communicated their ideas clearly in both technical and behavioral discussions and showed a professional approach throughout the interview process. Overall, the candidate performed well and made a positive impression.', '', 4.25, '2026-06-10 20:08:31', '2026-06-10 20:08:31'),
(394, 689, 0, 'Final', 'BNI Global', 'N/A', 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'Interview went ok. Gauri presented good analytical thinking and was able to identify the key business drivers behind revenue and profitability. During the case study, there were a few formula and reconciliation issues while building the model, but she took a structured approach to validate the assumptions, corrected the calculations, and ultimately arrived at the right conclusions with clear business insights.', '', 3.00, '2026-06-10 21:10:25', '2026-06-10 21:10:25'),
(395, 695, 0, 'Technical', 'niagarawater', 'N/A', 4, 4, 4, 4, 'Yes', 'Interview went well. Sudeeksha presented hands-on experience in robotics systems, sensor integration, perception, ROS2, and autonomous navigation. She was able to think through system design problems logically, ask relevant clarifying questions, and provide practical solutions while showing a good understanding of real-world deployment challenges and trade-offs.\nNext Steps: Continue strengthening knowledge around AI, Vision Language Models (VLMs), and modern inspection use cases involving foundation models, as these areas appear to be a growing focus for the team. Overall, the candidate presents a strong technical foundation and appears capable of contributing effectively to robotics and AI-driven automation initiatives.', '', 4.00, '2026-06-10 21:12:02', '2026-06-10 21:12:02'),
(396, 694, 0, '1st Tech', 'Corpay', 'NA', 4, 3, 3, 3, 'Yes', 'SQL basics', '', 3.25, '2026-06-10 21:16:10', '2026-06-10 21:16:10');
